window.SLATE_TEAMS_DOCS_INDEX = {"en":[{"t":"What SLATE Teams is","u":"01-what-is-teams.html","s":"Start","h":["The three things it is for","Five top-level tabs","How it relates to SLATE","Where your data is","Next"],"x":"SLATE Teams runs on your own machine . No server, nothing uploaded, model keys stay local. It makes one thing easy: several people and a crew of AI working at the same table — with a trace left behind for every decision. The wordmark is 席, which means both a seat at the table and the act of taking one. The interface follows the \"Ledger\" identity: graphite paper, red-ink annotations, square corners, hairline rules like a ledger page. The three things it is for Where What it owns Read --- --- --- Debate hall People and AI seats in one discussion; the host advances rounds; conclusions need a signature Team Office AI staff pick up work on their shift, every delivery passes a review, cost lands per employee Office Ledger Who said it, who approved it, how many tokens — stored, exportable, restorable Projects & data The debate hall is collaboration at the same moment — everyone in one discussion. The office is collaboration at different moments — you leave the work, an AI staff member does it on shift, you check it when you're back. Five top-level tabs - Office — one side is Chat (the ordinary one-to-one conversation: tool calls, approvals, context budget), the other is Desks (AI staff roster, duty schedule, hand-offs between desks, the delivery queue). Switch between them at the top right. - Team — the debate hall. Seats, the feed, and \"waiting for your signature\" in three columns. - Board — spread a discussion into a reasoning chain and workflow nodes. - Extensions — seven columns: skills, tools, reply modes, evolved tools, MCP, expert packs, Actions. What the model is allowed to use is decided here. - Settings — models, theme, language, data & privacy, and each token-spending AI feature. How it relates to SLATE SLATE Teams is a sibling of SLATE. They share the base — chat, tools, skills, board, data layer — and differ in the collaboration layer : multi-seat debates, tickets with narrowed scope, AI staff on a duty roster. Both install on one machine: ports, data directories, installer identity and update feeds are separate, so neither overwrites the other and no configuration is shared. If it's only you, SLATE is lighter. If you want people in the same discussion, or AI working by shift, use SLATE Teams. Where your data is Every conversation, seat, job, message and ledger entry lives in data/ inside the install directory as local SQLite files. Offline means no requests; the network is used only when you call a model API or check for updates. How to back it up — and why the two \"clear\" buttons are not the same thing — is in Projects & data. Next 1. Install & launch — set it up, add one model, open the first table. 2. Interface & tabs — what each of the five tabs holds, light and dark. 3. Office & AI staff — the part that is genuinely different here."},{"t":"Install & launch","u":"02-install.html","s":"Start","h":["Install","Windows","macOS","From source","Configure your first model","Coexisting with SLATE","If it won't start"],"x":"Install Windows Download SLATE-Teams-Setup-<version .exe , run it, and launch from the desktop icon. It installs into AppData\\Local\\Programs\\SLATE Teams for the current user and needs no administrator rights. The first launch opens a local window — that's the five tabs. macOS Releases ship SLATE Teams.app and SLATE-Teams-Setup-<version .dmg . From source, package it with build macos.sh in the repository, or just run python desktop.py (see \"From source\" below). The installed app keeps its data in ~/Library/Application Support/SLATE Teams , not inside the bundle. An unsigned build gets stopped by Gatekeeper once. Choose \"Open Anyway\" under System Settings → Privacy & Security; you only do this once. From source desktop.py starts the backend and opens the window itself. If you only want the API for another browser, run python backend/main.py and open http://127.0.0.1:<port / . Configure your first model Settings → model config (the \"管理模型密钥\" button in the header jumps straight there): fill in one provider's API key, pick a default model, and you're running. The key stays local — one copy in data/desktop state.json , one in browser state — and never appears in an outbound request, but it does travel with your backup . See the next box. The export packs in the whole local state, including model API keys in plaintext . A backup file is therefore a ring of keys: don't upload it to a drive, don't paste it into an issue, don't send it to anyone. To share a problem, send a screenshot and the log — nothing else. Coexisting with SLATE The two products can sit on one machine without overwriting each other: App port Data --- --- --- SLATE its own default data/ inside its own install SLATE Teams 8130 preferred, moves on if taken data/ inside its own install Installer identity, Start Menu entries and update feeds are all separate, so installing Teams can't hijack SLATE's auto-updates. If it won't start 1. Port taken : desktop backend.log in the data directory prints the port it actually got. 2. Missing dependencies : most common when running from source; the error names the package. More in FAQ."},{"t":"Interface & tabs","u":"03-interface.html","s":"Start","h":["The five tabs","The three columns of the team page","Theme","Interface language","Prompt Factory","Next"],"x":"One topbar over one workspace. Five tabs sit in the middle of the topbar; four buttons on the right: Keys , Remote , Theme , Settings . The five tabs Tab What it holds Read --- --- --- Office One page, two sides: Chat is the ordinary one-to-one conversation (sidebar, message feed, usage strip, input toolbar); Desks is the AI staff roster, the virtual office and the hand-off composer, with five tabs on the right: Activity / Waiting on you / Duties / Role / Standup & Record Chat & approvals · Office Team The debate hall: seats present, the feed, awaiting your signature Team Whiteboard Cards as a reasoning chain plus a freehand layer; five views: Git / Flow / Kanban / Outline / Workflow Whiteboard Extensions The master switch for everything the model may use, in seven sections: skills (SKILL.md), tools, modes, new features, MCP servers, expert packs, Actions Extensions Settings Models and keys, context and project, approval mode, theme, notifications, backup and storage, one block after another Settings The Office tab has a Chat / Desks switch at its top right, and it opens on Chat. Inside Chat, \"Project / Tasks / Summary\" is a column inside the page; switching them never leaves the conversation. The right rail stacks the task list, background tasks and the Grind panel, each opening and closing on its own. The three columns of the team page Three columns, one per question a meeting table asks: - Left · Present — who is at the table (AI seats and human seats), then \"Team preset\" and \"Team history\". History lives here too because both answer the same thing: how this session was assembled. - Middle · The feed — the topic field, the max round count, this session's usage strip, and two views underneath: Team discussion / Workflow. - Right · Awaiting You — the host-only actions: the \"Decisions need my sign-off\" switch and the items waiting on you. Theme Two built-in themes: light and dark . The \"Theme\" button in the topbar switches them; the shortcut is Ctrl+D ( ⌘D on macOS). Below that sits the custom theme (Settings → Custom theme): you fill only four source colors — page background, panel background, body text, accent — and the other thirty-odd tokens are derived from them by luminance and contrast, so every text level stays readable. The same block handles panel opacity, imported font files and a background image (or whatever Wallpaper Engine is currently showing). The preset row offers ten complete source sets: Ledger paper, Ink night, Mist blue, Deep sea, Pine ink, Moss, Clay, Dusk plum, Graphite, Letterpress. Clicking one fills the palette below; you can still edit each swatch — and once you do, it no longer belongs to any preset. While a custom theme is on, light/dark is locked: the topbar button and Ctrl+D do nothing, and clicking the button says why. Turning the custom theme off removes the whole injected stylesheet, down to the pixel. Interface language There is no language switch inside the app. The language is chosen at install time; the installer writes it to data/language.txt ( zh or en ) and the runtime only reads it. To change it: edit data/language.txt , or start with the SLATE LANG environment variable (higher priority), then restart. Translation covers interface text only — including button tooltips and input placeholders. Model output, your own input and code blocks are never translated. Prompt Factory It no longer owns a tab. The entry is the Open Workbench button under Settings → Context & Project . The factory folds the constitution summary, context snippets, task description, constraints and deliverable requirements into one prompt you can actually hand over. Closing it only hides the form: your draft, the files you ticked and the generated result are all still there when you reopen it. Next 1. Models & usage — add one model, read the usage strip. 2. Chat & approvals — how many approval modes there really are, and what each blocks."},{"t":"Models & usage","u":"04-models.html","s":"Daily","h":["Where models come from","Where keys are stored","The context budget","How to read the usage strip","Switching models and adding a vendor"],"x":"Where models come from The built-in list lives in the backend registry ( backend/routers/proxy.py ). The frontend fetches it at startup, in three groups: International models , Chinese Models , Local models . Recognising a vendor by its id prefix is enough: gpt- , claude- , gemini- , deepseek- , kimi- , qwen- , glm- , doubao- , MiniMax- , ernie- ; the local entry is simply id local (Ollama / LM Studio). Each vendor's request URL and declared context window are written in the registry — you never fill them. Some can be switched off, some force thinking (Kimi K3 and GLM-5.3 have no \"off\"), some only offer a bare toggle. The \"Reasoning effort\" control therefore shows a different set of stops per model. Where keys are stored Settings → Model Config → \"Built-in Model Keys\", one key per vendor; the Keys button in the topbar opens Settings directly. When you send, the local backend takes the key and authenticates against that vendor. Keys land in data/desktop state.json under modelKeys , with a copy in the browser's local state. The LAN remote reads that same file, so configuring it once covers the phone too. Settings says it plainly: a backup is \"a single JSON file containing the backend database and local settings\". Local settings include modelKeys . Treat the backup file as a secret — no group chats, no public cloud drive, never commit it to a repository. The context budget The denominator of that percentage is not the model's declared window — it is this session's budget : - \"Auto\" (the default) = the model's declared window × 0.8 , floored, not snapped to a slider stop . - Only models with no window information at all fall back to the global \"Context Token Limit\" (64000 by default). - A value you set by hand wins, but never above that model's declared window. The 20% is for output. Snapping to whole stops would flatten 128K / 200K / 256K into one number, and a small-window model can't reach the lowest stop at all — it would return 0 and occupy the full window with no room left to answer. The same budget feeds two places: where the context bar counts as full, and which round auto-compaction fires on. One number, so \"it compacted while still under the limit\" cannot happen. To tune one model: \"Max context\" on its row in Model Config — the slider rough-selects, the number box takes an exact value, and local or custom endpoints can \"Probe window\" to ask the endpoint itself. When budget and declared window disagree, the usage strip's hover shows both numbers. How to read the usage strip The strip above the conversation, left to right: Segment What it is --- --- Model name The current model; a warning mark appears beside it when no key is set Messages Message count for this conversation In Cumulative prompt tokens Out Cumulative completion tokens Total The two summed Context Tokens in use, plus a progress bar for the share of budget The Context segment is clickable and jumps to that model's budget slider in Settings. Hovering the strip expands Context Breakdown into five buckets: System Prompt / Tool Catalog / Skill Injection / Tool Calls & Results / Messages, each with its share. Tokens are estimated at roughly 3 characters per token. Trust the share and the trend, not a line-by-line match with your upstream bill. Switching models and adding a vendor - Switch model : the model dropdown in the chat input toolbar. It is one global setting — changing conversation does not change the model, though each conversation keeps its own usage counters. - Add a vendor : Settings → Model Config → \"+ Add Model\". Three request modes: OpenAI-compatible (appends /chat/completions itself), Anthropic ( /v1/messages + x-api-key ), or raw curl (Base URL is the full endpoint). Then fill Base URL, API Key (optional) and Context Window. - Backup & restore : Settings → Data Backup & Restore merges by id and does not overwrite existing data. Details in Projects & data."},{"t":"Chat & approvals","u":"05-chat-approval.html","s":"Daily","h":["What the Office chat view does","Approval modes: four of them","What Night Mode actually means","Where the high-risk lists live","What the approval dialog shows","How tool calls render","Next"],"x":"What the Office chat view does Open Office in the top bar and you land here by default. The switch at the top right goes to Desks — the AI staff office. They are two sides of one page, not two separate tables. - Sidebar , three tabs: Project (folder and file tree), Tasks (past conversations — searchable, batch manageable, archivable), Summary. - Above the feed : manual context compaction, memory & profile, expert packs, prompt snippets, task list, background tasks. - Input toolbar, left : the \"+\" popover — Grind Mode, Brainstorm, Target Mode, Scheduled Tasks, plus Mentions (@ prefix) for skills / tools / MCP / files. Then response mode, approval mode, attachment, model, reasoning effort. - Input toolbar, right : Polish prompt, Voice Input, Send. Enter sends, Shift+Enter breaks a line. Four built-in response modes: Smart, Chat, Economy, Turbo. They differ in whether the tool catalog goes out, how many rounds they get and which prompt they append; custom modes live on the Extensions page. Approval modes: four of them The pill at the lower left of the input box is approval mode. There are four , changeable at any time, and the change applies to this conversation only : id Label Lets through Stops --- --- --- --- ask Manual Approval Tools that never cross this gate, like local file reads and writes Asks before every command and every network call auto Auto Approval Commands and network calls matching no high-risk rule Asks only when one does full Full Access Never asks for commands or network Still asks when a condition is missing; catastrophic commands stay hard-blocked night Night Mode Commands, network and questions all go unanswered Only catastrophic commands ask is the default for new conversations. Settings → Approval Mode changes that default; a conversation that has picked one stops following it. terminal running a command, bg task starting a job (status / log / stop change nothing, so they don't count), web search, web fetch, browser automation. Local file reads and writes never come here. What Night Mode actually means The unattended tier: the same pass-through rule as Full Access, plus the \"ask one multiple-choice question when a condition is missing\" path switched off too. No question pops — the model picks an option itself, writes the choice and its reason into its reply, and continues. It adds no new rule and opens no new door — the only difference is that nothing is waiting for a person. Pair it with \"Keep the system awake while Night Mode tasks run\" (Settings → Approval Mode, on by default). The backend refuses these prefixes with no override, approval included: rm -rf / , rm -rf ~ , format c: , format d: , mkfs , dd if= . Full Access is marked red (no safety net); Night Mode night purple (the night is handed over). Where the high-risk lists live One list, mirrored on both sides — change both or they drift: - Frontend: HIGH RISK PATTERNS in frontend/js/services/riskguard.js , plus one check for \"downloaded and piped straight into a shell\". - Backend: HIGH RISK PATTERNS in backend/skills/terminal.py (one more rule, the PowerShell ri alias) and BLOCKED PREFIXES . The rules are hard-coded: file and directory deletion, disk writes and partitioning, shutdown and reboot, privilege escalation, forced kills, the registry, services and accounts, file permissions, Git force-push / hard reset / clean / branch delete, database drops and truncates, global dependency removal. Each command is split on && , , ; and and checked segment by segment, so a rule buried in a chain cannot slip through. What the approval dialog shows Three titles: High-Risk Command Approval / Command Approval / Network Access Approval. It states the triggered rule or the current mode, prints the command or the access target, and for commands has the current model explain what the command does (turn that off under Settings → AI features). The button reads \"Approve & Run\" or \"Allow access\". Under parallel runs several dialogs queue rather than quietly refusing each other, so nothing is rejected before you've seen it. A refusal goes back to the model verbatim, with an explicit instruction not to retry the same call. How tool calls render Each call is a card: tool icon, name, a one-line summary, and a status pill reading executed, applied, created, appended, diff preview, file preview, append preview, failed, or not run. Cards are collapsed by default ; only a failed one opens on its own. Click for the arguments and output — for file edits that means the path and the edit count, never the whole diff. Images, videos and documents a tool produced get a preview inside the card, and several calls in one turn group under a heading reading \"{n} calls\", listing the first three tool names. Next - To have AI keep working while you're away: Office. - How the context budget is computed: Models & usage."},{"t":"Team · the debate hall","u":"06-team.html","s":"Collaborate","h":["Seats","How one discussion runs","Board workflows","Every line is kept","Next"],"x":"Team is the top-level tab next to Office , and it is a table: several people and several AI seats in one discussion, a host advancing the rounds, and a conclusion that a human signs . Three columns side by side — seats present on the left, the feed in the middle, what needs you on the right. Seats - AI seats — picked from your models; the host decides who speaks first and for how many rounds. - Human seats — press \"添加真人席位\" (add a human seat) to issue a ticket , then send the join link. The other person opens it in their own browser and sees this discussion only — nothing else on your machine. The ticket decides which discussion a person may enter. When it expires or is revoked, their page says so plainly (\"票据已失效，请让主持人重新发一张\" — the ticket is no longer valid, ask the host for a new one) instead of hanging on a spinner. Seat state is visible in the left column: online , away , not joined , timed out without speaking . You never have to guess who is missing. How one discussion runs 1. The host opens it; the first round starts speaking, and the feed gets a rule —— 第 1 轮 —— (\"round 1\"). 2. Each round, seats speak in turn; anyone can reply to a named seat (\"回应 {name}\"). 3. In the final round the heading is 最终决策 (final decision) — that entry is not a conclusion, it is a proposal waiting for your signature . 4. The stop point reads \"等待你拍板\" (waiting for your call) and offers two buttons: 采纳拍板 (adopt it) or 继续讨论 (keep discussing). Adopting records \"已采纳这个决策\" (this decision was adopted) and stores who signed it. A human seat has two settings: permission (may they speak, may they call it) and what to do when they don't show (let AI write for them / skip and leave a trace / keep waiting, with a timeout in seconds). The invite link is issued from the same panel. The participant side uses different words: when it's their turn the page says \"现在轮到你发言\" (it's your turn to speak), typing early tells them \"发言会在轮到你时被采纳\" (your message will be picked up on your turn), and otherwise it shows \"等 {name} 发言…\" (waiting for {name}). Their positions are: 提案 (propose), 支持 (support), 反对 (oppose), 反驳 (rebut), 补充 (add to), 决策 (decide). Only the entry you signed counts as the conclusion. In night mode (full autopilot) the system adopts for you, and the feed states it explicitly: \"夜间模式：决策已自动采纳\". That is the exception, not the default. Board workflows The Team tab can also run a workflow drawn on the board: nodes execute one by one with progress written as {ok}/{n} 节点成功 (nodes succeeded), and a failure stops there to say which node broke — it never passes a half-run off as success. Every line is kept Speech, rounds, signatures and tool calls are stored locally and travel with your backups (the four debate tables are listed in Projects & data). Moving machines, restoring history, or clearing one discussion alone all follow the two different rules in that chapter. Next - To have work finished while you are away: Office. - To see the tool calls behind each message: Chat & approval."},{"t":"Office · hiring, rosters, deliveries","u":"07-office.html","s":"Office","h":["What the panel looks like","Hiring","Scheduling","The delivery queue","Next"],"x":"The office is collaboration at different moments : you leave a piece of work, an AI staff member does it on their shift, you check it when you are back. It does not add a background service — the open SLATE Teams page is what executes . The top-level Office tab opens on the Chat side; this chapter is about switching to Desks . The switch sits at the top right, and both sides stay on the same page. The backend only queues; it never executes work itself. So the office needs one machine with SLATE Teams open: that page is whoever is on duty. With the app closed, jobs sit quietly in the queue until a page is back. What the panel looks like Roster on the left with a floor plan of the desks (who's busy, who's free, who is handing something over), a message box in the middle that can \"交给\" (assign to) one employee, \"贴出来\" (post for everyone) or \"交办\" (hand over a job), and five tabs on the right: 动态 (feed), 等你拍板 (waiting on you), 值班表 (duties), 岗位 (roles), 站会与绩效 (standup & record). This chapter covers roles and duties; the last two live in Working like a person and Gates & accounts. Hiring Under Hire there are two ways in: \"Hire from a template\" (four built in: researcher, engineer, reviewer, duty keeper), or fill in a new colleague from scratch. Each employee carries these fields: Field What it decides --- --- Name / avatar / hue Colleagues address each other by name — names must be unique One line describing the role / 目标 (goal) / Duties What they do and what they aim at; also what triage weighs when deciding if a job is theirs Model / rounds / project Which model, how many turns one run may take, which project root the work lands in the reviewer Whether a delivery passes a human and who reviews it; \"No reviewer (deliveries come straight to you)\" ships it to you Daily budget How many tokens per day before the breaker trips (see Gates & accounts) Unattended Which approval level their shifts run at \"解雇\" (fire) takes them off the roster — the jobs they did and the things they said stay in the account , and their record row is marked 已离职 (left). Scheduling \"Add duty\" puts a shift on an employee. Two kinds of trigger: - Daily / every N minutes / once — the clock comes to look. - Event Trigger — a commit landed, watched paths changed, a self-check script went red, a Git push, or an external callback. The clock firing is not the same as \"act now\". Each shift can carry a Guard , most often: - \"No more than a few tasks pending\" — set to 0 and it means only move when my hands are empty . - \"Only schedule inside this window\". When a guard can't be read, or a condition type is no longer understood, the panel shows that as a line of text instead of silently skipping. Firing on time lets one employee pick up another job before finishing the last, and the queue just grows. A guard turns \"should I move\" into a check with a readable answer. The delivery queue Each employee on the roster shows one state — Idle , Working , Off duty — followed by counters: pending, waiting on you, awaiting review, returned, budget spent. Job states are few enough to just learn: State Meaning --- --- Queued · {when} Scheduled, waiting for an open page to claim it Working A page holds it under a lease; if that page dies, the job is claimable again {n} awaiting review Done, waiting for the reviewer Waiting on you Listed under \"Waiting on you\" — it needs your call Blocked Stuck, and the line says what it is blocked on Settled / {n} failed Finished / broke, with the reason on that line Every \"didn't happen\" has to produce a line you can read. There is no silent retry and no silent discard. Next - How they remember the last run and decide a job isn't worth doing: Working like a person. - Review, budget, deadlines, standup and record: Gates & accounts."},{"t":"Office · working like a person","u":"08-office-work.html","s":"Office","h":["He remembers the last run","Morning triage","\"Not worth doing\" needs your nod","Hand-offs between desks","Next"],"x":"If a duty roster were only \"wake the model when the clock says so\", it would be a cron job. This layer exists so an employee remembers the last run, orders their own queue, says why something didn't happen, and can hand work to a colleague . He remembers the last run Every employee keeps their own notes, written with \"Leave yourself a note\", readable only by that employee at the start of their next run. Three kinds: - open — something not finished yet. - ledger — the conclusion of a finished thing. - blocked — what condition is missing before it can move. At the start of a run those three piles appear as 未闭环 (open) / 卡住 (stuck) / 已定论 (settled), most recent first. When a thing is genuinely finished, write a ledger note and cross out the matching open note. Leave it and the next run does the same thing again — not a bug, but the direct consequence of \"memory only holds what he wrote down\". Morning triage Triage orders the jobs under his own name , one batch at a time: Action Meaning --- --- keep Worth doing. Priority 0–9, higher gets claimed first; optionally with a deadline defer Hold it, look again tomorrow drop Judged not worth doing — a reason is mandatory Triage can only touch his own queue, never anyone else's. \"Not worth doing\" needs your nod An employee may judge a job pointless, but that judgement does not take effect : after a drop the job parks under \"Waiting on you\", where you get two buttons: - Agree it should not be done, close it out — accept the judgement, the job is settled. - Not right — put it back — overrule it, the job returns to the queue. Same shape when a run can't continue: \"Close out this run\" has exactly two statuses, each with its own door for you: - Blocked — the missing condition is written on the line; supply it and press \"补齐条件，放回队列\" (fill in the condition, put it back). - Judged not worth doing — the reason is on the line; it only settles when you nod. Both wait for a human. No job ever disappears quietly. Hand-offs between desks \"Message a Colleague\" turns one sentence into a new job scheduled under the other employee — you don't wait for a reply. The recipient is one of three things: - a colleague's name or employee id; - user — said to you only, it lands in your notifications; - broadcast — pinned to the office feed where everyone sees it. One message, one thing to do: say what is wanted, don't paste the process. Hand-offs are counted: the feed shows 第 1 手 / 第 2 手 (\"hop 1\", \"hop 2\"…), counting round trips between colleagues. At hop 6 nothing gets woken automatically — the message is still left there. That rule exists so two colleagues can't kick a ball to each other forever. Deadline reminders the clock raises don't count as a hop: a clock has no round trip. Next Review gate, daily budget, deadline escalation, standup and record are the four things that keep this in check: see Gates & accounts."},{"t":"Office · gates & accounts","u":"09-office-gates.html","s":"Office","h":["The review gate","Daily budget","Expired deadlines escalate to a human","Two cards","Next"],"x":"Handing work to AI staff needs a few gates: deliveries shouldn't land on you unexamined, spend has to have a ceiling, and an expired deadline shouldn't rot on the desk. All four live in this layer, and every number is computed from the same jobs table — there is no second ledger. The review gate When you hire someone you pick \"the reviewer\" for them. Their deliveries go to that reviewer first and not straight to you . - Review is itself a job scheduled under the reviewer : it shouldn't sit behind ordinary duty work, so it queues slightly ahead — but anything triage raised above it still goes first. Its deadline defaults to two hours. - The reviewer closes it with \"Judge This Delivery\", and there are exactly two verdicts: approve (it passes, and this is the first time the delivery reaches you) or return (it fails, back to the author, with what to change written down). - The reviewer must exist in the roster, cannot review themselves , and cannot review for someone who has left the roster. Before review passes you only get \"An employee sent a delivery for review\"; after it passes you get \"Employee delivery\". When it comes back the line reads \"Returned in review: why\". That split is deliberate — something that hasn't passed shouldn't look like a delivery . A returned job is re-done through the same hand-off channel, so it counts in \"hop {n}\" too and stops at hop 6. Daily budget Each employee can carry a Daily budget in tokens. Once today's spend reaches it: - the duty roster schedules no new work , and the job shows up as Blocked with the reason on the line; - morning triage and your own \"Run now\" still schedule . Otherwise a full budget would lock you out of even asking them to finish the last item in hand. The record column reads \"{used today} / cap {budget}\" and marks Budget spent once it's over. Expired deadlines escalate to a human If triage gave a job a deadline, the clock speaks for the human once it passes: a system line appears in the feed and the job moves into \"Waiting on you\". The same reminder fires once — refreshing doesn't nag you again — and each pass escalates only a handful of jobs, because flooding the feed is the same as not reminding anyone. Two cards Today's standup — every shift that had \"Morning triage\" checked leaves one self-reported line: who, what they said, when. If nobody has reported it says so and tells you to put a triage shift on someone, rather than showing you an empty table. Record — one row per employee: {n} done, {n} failed, {n} waiting on you, {n} awaiting review, {n} returned, how long a run takes on average, and how many tokens went today. That column spans claim to close-out , not end-to-end wall clock — time spent waiting in the queue isn't counted. It's an order of magnitude, not a receipt. Next How these jobs, messages and verdicts get into a backup: Projects & data."},{"t":"The board and workflows","u":"10-board.html","s":"Capabilities","h":["How cards form a logic chain","The workflow view on the board","DAG workflows run on the Team tab","Next"],"x":"The board is the fourth tab in the top bar, and it is one global board: cards, connectors, freehand strokes and text notes stack as four layers on one canvas. It is not split per conversation — its contents are stored with your local settings and are still there when you switch. How cards form a logic chain A card carries four things: a title , a description , a colour tag , and arrow targets (target card IDs, comma-separated). Double-click a card to edit it in place, drag it to move it, or use the connect tool and click two cards to add an edge. Colour is not decoration: red is risk, orange to do, yellow an idea, green done, blue information, purple creative, default unclassified. Arrows express dependency and data flow. The kanban view columns cards by colour, the flow view links them into a graph, the outline view collapses parent-child levels, and the Git view reads your repo's commits. All five view buttons sit in the board header and it opens on kanban . The toolbar adds pen and text as free layers, with undo-stroke and clear-strokes; header buttons are add card, auto-arrange layout, return to content, AI-organise into a flow chart, show/hide the flow chart (Mermaid), export, clear. \"AI-organise into a flow chart\" is one of the AI-assisted features. Turn it off and the button only explains why — it never sends your board to a model. The workflow view on the board This column is not a DAG editor. It is three things on one screen: 1. A run control bar — state reads 空闲 (idle), 运行中 · 第 {n} 轮 (running, round n), 已完成 (done), 已中断 (aborted), with elapsed time beside it, and buttons for stop, run it out, auto-advance, reply mode, thinking effort and \"go to team\". When this conversation has never run, the list keeps a line saying 本场还没有运行记录 instead of leaving the previous run's tail on screen. 2. Current run — every tool call this round, with status 进行中 / 完成 / 失败 / 已取消 , under a heading of 当前运行 · {finished}/{total} . 3. Process-spec cards — one Action per card, labelled 共 {n} 步 (n steps), {n} 项输入 (n inputs), 产出落到… (output lands in …). Expand its steps in place, press 运行此流程 to send it into the conversation as an @-mention, or pin it. The author line reads 用户编写 (written by you) or 模型编写 (written by the model). Below them sits the team star map : the conversation is the centre star, each member a planet, real hand-offs between members drawn as arcs. With no team record for this conversation it says so plainly and tells you where to start one. DAG workflows run on the Team tab The thing that executes node by node lives in the workflow column of the Team tab — a tab beside \"team debate\". - Definitions are JSON files; 8 ship built-in under backend/workflows/ , and an empty list writes the path to drop them in on the screen. - The task goes in first and reaches every node as $input ; without it the run refuses to start and says so. - Node states read 等待 / 运行中 / 成功 / 失败 / 跳过 ; nodes with no dependency between them run in parallel , and progress reads 运行中（{done}/{n}）… . - The finished line is {ok}/{n} 节点成功 · 产物已写入知识库（{title}），可在记忆面板查看 — \"{ok}/{n} nodes succeeded, output written to the knowledge base, viewable in the Memory panel\". If every node passed but the write failed, it becomes 节点成功 {ok}/{n}，但写入知识库失败: {msg} : a half run is never reported as success . - A failed or skipped upstream node skips everything downstream and names who was responsible. A cycle is reported as DAG 存在环，涉及节点: {nodes} and that workflow does not run. - A node bound to neither a team member nor an explicit model falls back to the default set under \"AI-assisted features → team workflow execution\"; a bound node keeps its own binding. A node with no usable model fails outright. Each run becomes one entry titled 工作流产物 · {workflow} carrying every node's status, elapsed time, error and output summary. Find it in the memory panel — not on the board. Next - Creating and rolling back an Action: Extensions. - The switch and default model for workflow execution: Settings."},{"t":"Extensions","u":"11-extensions.html","s":"Capabilities","h":["Skills and tools are not the same thing","Reply mode","Expert pack","MCP and Actions","Next"],"x":"Extensions is the fifth tab in the top bar, and its subtitle states the whole remit: the capabilities available to a model are decided on this page . The left rail holds seven columns, each with a count; the rail number and the heading number come from one source, so they change together. Column What it governs What you can do --- --- --- Skills A written \"how to do this kind of job\" note for the model (SKILL.md) Create, import from a local path, import from a GitHub repo, discover plugins in standard directories, delete, open one and try it Tools Resident backend capabilities, called through skill run Read-only list, open one to run it; built-in tools cannot be deleted Modes Reply modes Four built-in tiers read-only; custom modes added, edited, deleted New capabilities Tools SLATE generated for itself, under data/evolved/ Enable / disable, roll back, revoke (source goes to history first) MCP Remote tools brought by external MCP servers Add, connect / disconnect, delete, enable or disable per project Expert packs Persona + rules + knowledge base + skills bundled as one switchable expert Create, import a zip, export, add or remove files inside Actions Process specifications Create, edit, delete, roll back Skills and tools are not the same thing A skill is one SKILL.md: you write in plain language how this kind of job should be done, and after import the model picks it up by task. 6 sample skills ship with the product (code review, commit message, design, research, weekly report, Windows troubleshooting). Tools are capabilities implemented in backend code. This column lists the 35 entries of the built-in registry — reading and editing files, terminals and background tasks, generating PPT/Word/Excel/PDF, browser and desktop automation, web search and page fetching. They are read-only here. What you can switch off is the set of features that call a model on their own, under Settings: a capability switched off does not even appear in the model's tool catalogue. A separate group of in-conversation tools (board read/write, passing work between desks, creating reply modes, closing out a target mode) is not listed there; the reply mode's tool whitelist decides those. Use the tool factory (built-in tool mcp factory ) to generate one. It lands in data/evolved/ and shows up in the New capabilities column, where it can be disabled, rolled back or revoked at any time. Every overwrite, revocation and rollback stores the previous content first; up to 5 versions are kept. Reply mode A reply mode decides which prompt set this conversation uses, which tools are open, how many rounds it runs, how hard it thinks and which model answers . The four read-only built-ins are smart (full tool set), chat (no tools at all, one round), economy (read-only tools only — it can see the project and skill catalogues but cannot write, run a command or spend generation quota; low effort, 12 rounds) and turbo (full tool set, high effort, 40 rounds, no stopping to ask). A custom mode is a full specification: id, display name, icon, colour, appended prompt, tool whitelist ticked item by item, reasoning effort, round limit and a chosen model (follows the current main model by default). The model can create modes too — it calls mode write , and the result lands in the same registry as your manual edits. Above the input box you change which mode this conversation uses ; in the \"Modes\" column you change what the mode itself is . Deleting a custom mode that is in use breaks nothing — those conversations fall back to the default mode. Approval mode (manual / auto / full access / night) is a different mechanism governing whether commands and network access ask you first ; its default is set in Settings, and Chat & approval covers it. Expert pack One expert pack = persona + behaviour rules + knowledge-base files + skill files, bundled as a single switchable whole. 3 sample packs ship with the product. Two ways to use one: pick it from the expert selector under the input box to inject it into this conversation, or attach it to an AI seat in the Team tab. MCP and Actions The MCP column connects to external servers; once connected their remote tools enter the model's view, and a remote tool sharing a built-in name is overridden by the built-in. Each server can be disabled globally or enabled/disabled for the current project alone (a project mask) — removing the mask returns it to the global configuration. Actions are process specifications : routine operations written as required steps, which the model then follows. They are stored as data/actions/<id .yml , or in a project's own .slate/actions/ where a same-named project Action wins. Every overwrite keeps a backup, up to 5 versions, and can be rolled back; a stored version that no longer parses is not allowed to be written back. In the board's workflow view, one Action is one runnable card. Next - Which features call a model on their own, and how to switch each off: Settings."},{"t":"Projects, backups and the ledger","u":"12-projects-data.html","s":"Data & settings","h":["Projects and workspaces","What a backup actually carries","Two ordering traps when restoring","The two \"clear\" actions are not the same","What stays out of the JSON on purpose","Next"],"x":"Teams keeps its things in three layers: the view (which project you're looking at), the records (tables in the chat database) and the configuration (files under data/ , plus the .slate/ inside your project). One backup moves only part of the first two. Projects and workspaces - A single-folder project is just that folder. A workspace is a host folder holding the configuration, whose members are several unrelated folders. The host lands at data/workspaces/<name , its configuration is <host /.slate/config.json , holding three things: what it is, the member list, the current root. - There is one current root at a time . Switching it changes that one value; files, Git and the terminal working directory follow. Where configuration gets read and written is tracked separately, so a workspace's settings never land in a member's own .slate/ . - Everything registered stays in data/projects.json , and the one you're looking at is still unique. Identity comes from the absolute path of the host folder — move it and the identity changes, which is why each entry carries aliases to re-file old conversations by hand. - Conversations attach to a project id , not a name. SLATE's own per-project data goes to data/projects/<id / , never into your repo. What a backup actually carries An export is one JSON file with a version number and three parts: the backend tables, your browser's local blob, and the team history list. Group Tables Inside --- --- --- Chat conversations, messages sessions and messages, archived ones included Memory memories, prompt snippets long-term memory, prompt material Four debate tables team sessions, team turns, team attendees, team inbox each debate's header and seat snapshot, full speech text, tickets (sha256 only), turns waiting to be collected Two ledger tables runs, tool events the accounts per pass and every tool call; the star map and \"which files changed\" count from here Two office tables office jobs, office messages the delivery queue and desk messages Daily accounts daily usage tokens per day; without it sessions restore fine and the activity heatmap stays blank Three roster tables employees, employee duties, employee notes AI staff, duty schedules, their own notes A missing table always shows up the same way: the backup looks complete, and that block is empty after the restore . So every new table declares itself — record or configuration. Two ordering traps when restoring - Create the tables first, then merge. The debate, ledger and office tables are built lazily by whichever endpoint touches them first, so on a clean machine that never opened the team tab and never hired anyone they don't exist at all. Skip that and they all read as \"no data\": the count comes back 0 while the screen still says \"done\". - Merge only what's new. Rows go in by primary or natural key; an existing row is skipped, never overwritten. The speech and tool-event tables drop their row numbers first — the same utterance is the same (session, sequence) pair on both machines, and reusing the id would collide with a locally written row and get silently swallowed. - The page reloads once after an import: the local half only takes effect on reload. The two \"clear\" actions are not the same Where you click What goes What stays --- --- --- Task list, \"clear all sessions\" Sessions and messages The debate text and delivery history, with only their references to these sessions blanked out Settings, storage, \"clear conversations\" Messages, sessions, the four debate tables, the two ledger tables, the two office tables, the daily accounts — then the database is compacted Employees, duty schedules and their notes; memory and prompt material; the knowledge base The confirmation has to say that in full. The roster and the schedules are configuration , not history: nobody says \"clear conversations\" meaning \"fire my staff and cancel their shifts\". What stays out of the JSON on purpose Configuration and binaries under data/ aren't backed up: desktop state.json , mcp servers.json (MCP endpoints and secrets), scheduled tasks.json , skills/ , experts/ , actions/ , constitution.json , knowledge.db , data/theme/ (background images, imported fonts), the registry and its hosts. A project's own .slate/ travels with the code instead. The local half carries the model keys you typed in. Don't commit it, don't share it carelessly. Next - Keep working from another machine: Phone remote control. - Where the switches a backup doesn't carry live: Settings. - When something went wrong anyway: FAQ."},{"t":"Phone remote control","u":"13-mobile.html","s":"Data & settings","h":["What the phone has","What the phone doesn't have","How you get the phone screen","Where the switch lives","How to get the address","Headless mode","Why only the face changes","Next"],"x":"Remote control is the same backend with a different face : your phone's browser talks to the backend on your machine and drives the same engine — no second service, no second way of executing. What the phone has Five tabs: Chat , Chats (the session list), Memory , Tasks , Settings . - Streaming replies, collapsed reasoning and tool cards all work; tools really touch files (create, edit and append go through the same endpoints as on the desktop). - Approval became a bottom sheet: risky commands and file changes still need your nod, with a diff preview before anything lands. - Settings holds four things: the remote-control address with its QR code, model choice, keys, theme. Background-task events are read back into a finished pass as usual. What the phone doesn't have The Team , Office , Board and Extensions tabs exist on the desktop only. So: - You can't open a debate from a phone and can't see the delivery queue. A participant holding a ticket lands on another page entirely — that discussion and nothing else. - A phone page never claims office work . The backend only queues; the one on duty is the desktop page that is open, so with only a phone online an AI staff member's jobs sit quietly in the delivery queue. Files, Git, terminals and the ledger live on the host; put the host to sleep and nobody is working on the other end of that link. How you get the phone screen Open the address with its auth code on a phone and the page routes itself to the touch layout, keeping the code in the URL. Add slate mobile=0 to stay on the desktop layout. Where the switch lives Settings → LAN remote control → enable , and that is the only place. - The preference lives in data/desktop state.json . A missing file, a broken read or a missing key all mean on — defaulting to off would leave existing installs suddenly unreachable. - Turning it off really releases the listening port ; it doesn't just hide the address. - The switch is host-only . Flipping it from a device on the remote port is refused: that device is working through the very connection it would cut. How to get the address The settings block on the host lists the address with its auth code — copy it or scan the QR code. It is built from this machine's LAN IP and the port the side service actually got : it prefers one port and walks upward when that is taken, so don't hard-code the number anywhere else. The master auth code is generated fresh for every process, so a restart invalidates old links; a phone stuck on \"authorization required\" just needs a freshly copied address. Headless mode For machines with no desktop environment (a server, a Raspberry Pi, a container): no window, no tray — just the backend plus LAN remote control, with the local address and the authorized remote address printed to the terminal; Ctrl+C shuts it down. It forces remote control on for this process without writing the preference, and refuses to reuse a backend someone else started, because headless leaves no window to fix things with. A failed backend reports itself in the terminal. Why only the face changes The tool loop, message assembly, approval decisions and rendering logic all sit in the shared service modules; the phone injects only its own view and input. One engine behind two faces, so you never get \"it looked doable on the phone but ran something else\". The trade-off is honest too: debate and office interaction doesn't fit a touchscreen, so it isn't ported. Next - Tickets and the narrowed scope behind them: Team · the debate hall. - Why work waits for an open page: Office. - Switches a backup doesn't carry: Projects, backups and the ledger."},{"t":"Settings","u":"14-settings.html","s":"Data & settings","h":["Models and context","Custom theme","AI-assisted features","Why capability management isn't here","Data and devices"],"x":"Settings is the fifth tab in the top bar. The left column is an anchor navigation with a search box above it; the right column holds the grouped blocks. The navigation is read from the blocks at runtime , so the group count follows the version while the order always matches the main area. There are 21 groups : Models · API test · Usage · Context & project · Auto-advance · AI-assisted features · Notifications · Background tasks · Parallel runs & projects · Minimal UI (experimental) · Custom theme · Web search · Image generation · Video generation · Approval mode · Backup & restore · Session archive · Storage · LAN remote control · Typing game · About. Press Save at the top right to write everything. Interface language is not here : it is chosen at install time (written to data/language.txt ) and never switched inside the app, with precedence SLATE LANG that file Chinese. Models and context Models does two jobs: custom models (name/ID, request style — OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, or raw curl — Base URL, API Key, context window) and the keys for built-in models, plus an optional Responses API switch. API test fires one minimal request down the real chain — the same one a conversation uses, not a parallel one. Context & project decides how much a model can see at once. Built-in models and models with a declared window run on \"auto\", each taking eighty percent of its nominal window, so the global cap here is only a backstop for models with no window information; to tune one model, use the \"max context\" control on its row in Models — the slider is a rough pick, the number box beside it takes an exact value, and local or custom endpoints can probe the window . The compression threshold and the context meter compute from that same number. Then: a single-output cap of 1024–65536, with \"Raises the output length limit to 65536 when writing files so large files are not truncated\" on by default; \"auto-confirm file creation and modification\" on by default, and off it returns to preview-then-accept for every write; and the project constitution — standing hard rules for this project, with the prompt factory entry point in the same group. Custom theme With a custom theme enabled you fill in only four source colours (page background, panel, body text, accent); every other value is derived from them by luminance and contrast, so body text and the three secondary levels are pulled up to readable. The preset palette has 10 tiers : paper, ink night, mist blue, deep sea, pine, moss, clay, dusk plum, graphite, letterpress. A preset fills the four swatches and each stays editable — but once edited, the theme belongs to no preset . With a custom theme active, the top-bar light/dark button and Ctrl+D do nothing; pressing one tells you why. Switching the custom theme off returns the whole look to the built-in theme. - Fonts : families installed on the system are used by name. \"Import font\" takes one .woff2 / .woff / .ttf / .otf file up to 16MB and it lands only on this machine, under data/theme/fonts/ — not in conversation records, not in the repository, not in the installer, and it does not travel to another machine with a backup; with one weight imported, the browser fakes bold and italic. - Panel opacity (55%–100%) is a flat alpha on the panel, card, input and assistant-bubble layer: lowering it reveals the page colour or your wallpaper behind it, and it is not frosted-glass blur . Your own bubbles and code blocks always stay solid. - Background image is stored on this machine under data/theme/ , with a veil slider (40%–95%) — too low and body text sits on the picture, too high and the picture might as well not be there. The Wallpaper Engine row only reads that app's own configuration and preview image and uses it as your background; it does not start the app or change its settings. AI-assisted features Every feature that calls a model on its own — apart from conversation, team debate and the prompt factory — is in this group: 15 items , each with its own switch, and 12 of them can pick their own model. The other three carry no model picker because ownership differs: scheduled and event tasks choose a model inside each task ; image and video generation are configured in their own blocks. Switch an item off and no request is made for it again. The twelve are context compression summary, memory auto-distillation, manual memory extraction, conversation insight capture, automatic session title, code understanding document, code review, board AI organize, prompt polish, sub-agent parallelism, dangerous-command purpose explanation and team workflow execution. (The Auto-advance reviewer model and the background-task auto-resume are set in their own groups, not repeated here.) Why capability management isn't here Tools, skills, reply modes, expert packs, MCP servers and Actions all live on the Extensions tab — the single source of truth for the capability list. Settings keeps two kinds of thing: provider configuration for capabilities (the web-search engine and rendering mode, the image/video model and key) and the call gate (those 15 switches above). Each half of one concern stays in exactly one place. This page sets the default approval mode for new conversations (manual / auto / full access / night). A reply mode is a different thing, chosen per conversation above the input box. Data and devices Backup & restore exports one JSON (conversations, debates and the ledger, the staff roster and duty schedule, memories, assets, settings); restore merges by id and never overwrites what is there — Projects & data. Session archive holds archived sessions, restorable or deletable for good; Storage compacts the database and clears caches; LAN remote control serves this machine's address to a phone or tablet — see Mobile."},{"t":"FAQ","u":"15-faq.html","s":"Data & settings","h":["Won't start, won't connect","The interface","Office and debate hall","Data","Next"],"x":"Every answer here traces back to a line of code. Anything we couldn't verify isn't in this list. Won't start, won't connect Double-clicking does nothing, or the backend won't come up. If the first instance is still opening its window or is hiding in the tray, another launch calls it back and prints \"already running\". When it really fails, the port is usually taken: the app prefers 8130 and falls back to a free one, and remote control prefers 8131 and walks up twenty ports. Both use the port they actually got, so the address on screen is the truth and nothing else needs editing. Which file holds the logs. The backend and the launch sequence write desktop backend.log : at the repo root when running from source, next to the program folder on a Windows install, inside the data folder on a macOS install. Errors thrown by the page itself go to data/js errors.log . A phone opens the address and hits \"authorization required\", or it worked yesterday. The first case is an address without its auth code — copy it fresh from the host's settings or scan the QR code. The second is that the master auth code is generated anew for every process, so a restart retires the old link. Unauthenticated LAN access is refused on purpose. The interface How do I switch the interface language? You don't switch inside the app: the language is chosen at install time and written to data/language.txt . Edit that to en or zh , or override it once with the SLATE LANG environment variable, then restart. The red-ink side is hard to read in dark mode. Alert red, done green and to-do amber are not driven by your accent colour: a light set and a dark set exist and the page picks one by background luminance, custom themes included. The ledger red is deliberately deep and dull on light and swaps to a brighter value on dark, so \"darker means less visible\" never happens. Office and debate hall Why isn't an AI staff member's work running? The backend only queues; it executes nothing. The one on duty is the page that is open on that machine. Close every page and jobs stay in the queue; an expired lease returns a job to the queue, and the same job is claimed at most twice before it is declared failed. A phone page has no office, so a phone is never on duty. Where does work go once it is judged \"not worth doing\"? Into \"waiting on you\", with the reason written on the line. It isn't a failure and the backend never revives it: there are exactly two exits — you put it back in the queue (raised above ordinary duty work, though triage can still outrank it), or you agree it shouldn't be done and it closes. An employee can't open that door. The daily budget is full, so why did my own hand-off still schedule? The circuit breaker answers one question only: \"may the duty roster queue new work\". Already-queued jobs finish (cutting one half-way costs more and explains less), morning triage still runs — that is precisely the judgement of \"what to do with the budget left\" — and the button you pressed is your call to make. Why did the note get worked again on the next pass? That \"open item\" note was never struck through. When he writes a new note, he has to name the one it closes. Each person keeps only the forty most recent notes; unlimited history would fill his own context first. The participant's page says the ticket is no longer valid. Have the host issue a new one. Tickets can be revoked and the database stores only their hash, so a revoked link is dead for good — the original string can't be recovered from a backup either. Data \"Clear conversations\" left my staff in place, and a restore reported 0 rows. Both are designed. The roster, the duty schedules and an employee's own notes count as configuration , not history. A 0-row restore means that backup never carried the block: the tables are now created before merging so a clean machine doesn't silently drop whole pieces of history, but exports made before those tables existed genuinely have nothing to give back — export again. Is my key in the backup? Not in the backend half (the tables); yes in the local half, which is plaintext. Conversely, nothing under data/ that is configuration or a binary is in there: shared desktop settings, MCP endpoints and their secrets, scheduled tasks, skills, expert packs, action playbooks, the global constitution, the knowledge base, background images and imported fonts. Move those yourself. Next - Install methods and the port split: Install & launch. - The full backup scope: Projects, backups and the ledger. - Remote control and headless mode: Phone remote control."}],"zh":[{"t":"认识 SLATE Teams","u":"zh/01-what-is-teams.html","s":"开始","h":["三件核心的事","五个顶层页签","与 SLATE 的关系","数据在哪","下一步"],"x":"SLATE Teams 跑在 你自己的机器上 ：不需要服务器，不上传对话，模型密钥只存在本机。 它把一件事变得顺手——让几个人和一批 AI 在同一个桌面上协同，并且每一笔都留得下痕迹。 产品名里的「席」是双关：一张桌子上的座位，也是入席的那件事。界面走「席 · Ledger」这套视觉身份—— 石墨纸面、红墨批注、直角、账簿式的发丝分隔线。 三件核心的事 位置 它管什么 去这几章 --- --- --- 议事厅 真人席位与 AI 席位同开一场讨论，主持人推进轮次，结论要人拍板 团队 办公室 AI 员工按值班表自己找活干，交付要过审校，账算在每个人头上 办公室 账本 谁说的、谁批的、花了多少 token，全部落库可查可备份 项目与数据 议事厅是 同一时刻 的协同——大家在一场讨论里；办公室是 不同时刻 的协同—— 你把活留下，AI 员工在它值班时做完，你回来验收。 五个顶层页签 - 办公室 —— 一面是 对话 （常规的一对一会话，工具调用、审批、上下文预算都在这里）， 一面是 工位 （AI 员工名册、值班表、工位递话、交付队列）。右上角在两面之间切。 - 团队 —— 议事厅。席位栏、议事流、待你签字三栏并排。 - 黑板 —— 把讨论摊成逻辑链与工作流节点，看图推进。 - 扩展 —— 七栏能力：技能、工具、回复模式、新功能、MCP、专家包、Actions。模型能用什么，在这页定。 - 设置 —— 模型、主题、语言、数据与隐私、AI 辅助功能逐项开关。 与 SLATE 的关系 SLATE Teams 是 SLATE 的同源分支，共用底座（对话、工具、技能、黑板、数据层）， 差别在 协作层 ：多人席位、票据与作用域收窄、AI 员工与值班表。 两者可以在同一台机器上并存：端口、数据目录、安装器身份与更新源都是分开的， 互相不覆盖，也不共用一份配置。 只你一个人用，SLATE 更轻；要拉人一起讨论、或者想让 AI 按班次自己干活，用 SLATE Teams。 数据在哪 所有会话、席位、活与话、账本都在安装目录的 data/ 下，是本地 SQLite 文件。 不联网就不产生任何请求；联网只发生在你调用模型 API 与拉取更新时。 怎么备份、怎么清、哪两种「清空」不是一回事，写在 项目与数据。 下一步 1. 安装与启动 —— 装好、配一个模型、开第一桌。 2. 界面与页签 —— 五张页签各装什么，明暗两套主题。 3. 办公室与 AI 员工 —— 这一版最不一样的地方。"},{"t":"安装与启动","u":"zh/02-install.html","s":"开始","h":["装","Windows","macOS","源码","第一次配模型","与 SLATE 同机共存","起不来先看这两处"],"x":"装 Windows 下载 SLATE-Teams-Setup-<版本 .exe ，双击装完从桌面图标启动。默认装到当前用户的 AppData\\Local\\Programs\\SLATE Teams ，不需要管理员权限。 装完第一次启动会打开一个本地窗口，界面就是 五个页签。 macOS 发行版给的是 SLATE Teams.app 与 SLATE-Teams-Setup-<版本 .dmg ；从源码跑用仓库里的 build macos.sh 打包，或者 python desktop.py 直接起（见下面「源码」）。 装机版的数据目录不在应用包里，而在 ~/Library/Application Support/SLATE Teams 。 未签名的包会被 Gatekeeper 拦一下。在「系统设置 → 隐私与安全性」里点「仍要打开」， 只需要做一次。 源码 desktop.py 会自己起后端、自己开窗口；只想拿接口给别的浏览器用，用 python backend/main.py 起后端，然后开 http://127.0.0.1:<端口 / 。 第一次配模型 设置 → 模型配置 里填一家厂商的 API Key（顶栏那颗「管理模型密钥」直接跳到这一页）， 选一个默认模型，就能开了。Key 存在本机—— data/desktop state.json 与浏览器本地状态各一份—— 不会出现在任何一条对外请求里， 但它会跟着备份一起走 ，看下面那条。 导出的备份把整份本机状态一起打进去， 其中包含模型 API Key（明文） 。 所以备份文件等同于一串钥匙：不要上传到网盘、不要贴进 issue、不要发给别人。 要分享问题现场，只截界面图、只贴日志。 与 SLATE 同机共存 两个产品可以在同一台机器上并存，互不覆盖： 应用端口 数据 --- --- --- SLATE 各自的默认口 自己的安装目录 data/ SLATE Teams 首选 8130（被占则顺延） 自己的安装目录 data/ 安装器身份、开始菜单项、更新源都是分开的，所以不会出现\"装了 Teams 把 SLATE 的自动更新接走\"。 起不来先看这两处 1. 端口被占 ：日志 data/desktop backend.log 里会写它实际拿到的端口。 2. 依赖没装全 ：源码跑最常见，报错会直接说缺哪个包。 更多在 常见问题。"},{"t":"界面与页签","u":"zh/03-interface.html","s":"开始","h":["五个页签","团队页的三栏","主题","界面语言","提示词工厂","下一步"],"x":"界面是一张顶栏加一块工作区。顶栏中间排着五个页签，右边四颗按钮： 密钥 、 遥控 、 明暗 、 设置 。 五个页签 页签 它装什么 细写在哪 --- --- --- 办公室 一页两面： 对话 是常规的一对一会话（边栏、消息流、顶部用量条、输入区工具行）； 工位 是 AI 员工花名册、虚拟办公室与交办输入区，右侧五个页签：动态 / 等你拍板 / 值班表 / 岗位 / 站会与绩效 对话与审批 · 办公室 团队 议事厅：在场席位、议事流、等你拍板 团队 黑板 卡片式逻辑链与画笔层，五种显示视图：Git / 流程 / 看板 / 纲要 / 工作流 黑板 扩展 模型可用能力的总开关，七栏：技能 SKILL.md、工具、模式、新功能、MCP 服务、专家包、Actions 扩展 设置 模型与密钥、上下文与项目、审批模式、主题、通知、备份与存储，一块块往下排 设置 顶栏那颗「办公室」右上角有「对话 / 工位」切换；进页默认落在对话面。 对话面的左栏「项目 / 任务 / 总结」是页内边栏，切它们不会离开对话； 右边那一竖栏叠着任务清单、后台任务与磨墨面板，同样各管各的开合。 团队页的三栏 三栏是一张会议桌的形状，各回答一件事： - 左栏 · 在场 —— 谁在这桌上（AI 席位与真人席位），下面还有「团队预设」和「团队历史」。 历史名单同放左栏，因为两者读的是同一件事：这一场是怎么凑起来的。 - 中栏 · 议事流 —— 议题输入、最大辩论轮数、这一场的用量条，下面是「团队讨论 / 工作流」两个视图。 - 右栏 · 待你签字 —— 只有主持人能做的动作：「决策需我拍板」开关，以及等你处理的条目。 主题 内置两套： 浅色 与 深色 。顶栏「明暗」按钮切换，快捷键 Ctrl+D （macOS 上是 ⌘D ）。 再往下是 自定义主题 （设置 → 自定义主题）：只填四个源色——页面底色、面板底色、正文颜色、强调颜色， 其余三十几个色值由它们按亮度与对比度算出来，保证正文与三个次要层级都读得清。 同一页还能调板块透明度、导入字体文件、换背景图（或取 Wallpaper Engine 的当前壁纸）。 预设行给的是 十档 整套源色：簿纸、墨夜、雾蓝、深海、松墨、苔绿、陶土、暮紫、石墨、铅字。 点一档就把整套色填进色板，之后仍可逐格改——改过之后它就不再属于任何预设。 开启自定义主题期间明暗切换被锁住：顶栏按钮与 Ctrl+D 都不生效，点它会说明原因。 关掉自定义主题，整段注入的样式一起摘掉，一个像素都不留。 界面语言 应用内没有语言开关。 语言在安装时选定，安装程序把它写进 data/language.txt （ zh 或 en ），运行时只读。 要换语言：改 data/language.txt ，或者用环境变量 SLATE LANG 启动（优先级更高），然后重启。 翻译只作用于界面文字，连按钮的提示与输入框的占位符都算；模型生成的内容、你的输入、代码块不翻。 提示词工厂 它不再占一个页签。入口在 设置 → 上下文与项目 里那颗「打开工作台」。 工厂把宪法摘要、上下文片段、任务描述、约束与交付要求整合成一份可交付 Prompt。 收起只是加一层隐藏：再打开时已写的内容、勾过的文件、生成结果都还在。 下一步 1. 模型与用量 —— 配一个模型，看懂顶部那条用量栏。 2. 对话与审批 —— 审批到底几档，各档拦住什么。"},{"t":"模型与用量","u":"zh/04-models.html","s":"日常","h":["模型从哪来","密钥存在哪","上下文预算","用量条读法","换模型与加厂商"],"x":"模型从哪来 内置模型清单在后端的注册表里（ backend/routers/proxy.py ），前端启动时取过来填进选择器，分三组： 国际模型 、 国产模型 、 本地模型 。 按模型 id 的前缀认厂商就够了： gpt- 、 claude- 、 gemini- 、 deepseek- 、 kimi- 、 qwen- 、 glm- 、 doubao- 、 MiniMax- 、 ernie- ；本地那一条的 id 就叫 local （指向 Ollama / LM Studio）。 每家的请求地址与标称上下文窗口都写在注册表里，不用你填。 思考档位是按厂商给的：有的能关、有的是强制思考（Kimi K3、GLM-5.3 就没有「关」这一档）、 有的只有开关没有强弱。所以那颗「推理强度」滑杆上的档位会随模型变。 密钥存在哪 设置 → 模型配置 → 「内置模型密钥」逐家填；顶栏那颗「密钥」按钮直接打开设置页。 发请求时由本机后端拿着它去那家厂商鉴权。 它落在本机 data/desktop state.json 的 modelKeys 那一项里，浏览器本地状态同时存一份。 设置页写得很直白：备份是「后端数据库 + 本地设置」打成的单个 JSON 文件。本地设置就含 modelKeys 。 备份文件要当机密对待 ——别发到群里、别丢进公共网盘、别提交进仓库。 局域网遥控那侧读的是同一份 desktop state.json ，配过一次，手机跟着走。 上下文预算 用量条那个百分比的分母不是模型标称窗口，是 这一场的预算 。口径只有一条： - 「自动」 （默认档）= 该模型标称窗口 × 0.8 ，向下取整， 不吸附到滑杆档位 。 - 窗口完全缺失的模型，才用设置里那个「上下文 Token 上限」兜底（默认 64000）。 - 你手动设过的值优先，但不会超过该模型的标称窗口。 为什么留两成：剩下的要给输出。吸附到整档会把 128K / 200K / 256K 压成同一个数， 更麻烦的是小窗口模型凑不满最低一档只能返回 0，等于全额占满窗口、一点输出余量都不留。 预算同时喂给两处： 上下文条算到哪儿算满 、 自动压缩在第几轮触发 。两边是同一个数， 所以不会出现「看着没满就压缩了」。 要单独调某个模型：模型配置里该行的「最大上下文」，滑杆粗选、旁边的数字框填精确值； 本地与自定义端点还能「探测窗口」，让程序去问端点自己报多大。预算与标称窗口不一致时， 用量条的悬浮层会把两个数都写出来。 用量条读法 对话面会话区上方那条，从左到右： 段 它是什么 --- --- 模型名 当前模型；没配密钥时旁边亮一个警告标 消息 这一场的消息条数 输入 累计 prompt token 输出 累计 completion token 总计 两者之和 上下文 已占用 token 数 + 占预算的百分比进度条 「上下文」那一段可以点，点了直接跳到设置页这一档的预算滑杆。停在用量条上会展开 上下文构成 ， 按五个桶分：系统提示词 / 工具目录 / Skill 注入 / 工具调用与结果 / 对话消息，各带占比。 token 按约 3 字符 / token 估。可信的是占比与趋势，不是与上游账单逐位一致。 换模型与加厂商 - 换模型 ：对话面输入区工具行的模型下拉。它是全局的一档——切会话不会换模型， 但每场对话各自记着自己的用量。 - 加厂商 ：设置 → 模型配置 → 「+ 添加模型」。请求模式三种：OpenAI 兼容（自动拼 /chat/completions ）、 Anthropic（ /v1/messages + x-api-key ）、curl 直连（Base URL 填完整端点地址）；再填 Base URL、 API Key（可选）、Context Window。 - 备份与恢复 ：设置 → 数据备份与恢复，按 id 合并导入，不覆盖已有数据。详见 项目与数据。"},{"t":"对话与审批","u":"zh/05-chat-approval.html","s":"日常","h":["办公室的对话面能做什么","审批模式：四档","夜间模式到底是什么","高危清单在哪","审批框长什么样","工具调用在界面上怎么呈现","下一步"],"x":"办公室的对话面能做什么 从顶栏「办公室」进入，默认就在这一面；右上角可以切到「工位」——那是 AI 员工的办公室， 两边是同一页的两面，不是两张桌子。 一列边栏、一条会话区、一行输入区。 - 边栏 三个页签：项目（目录与文件树）、任务（历史会话，可搜索、批量管理、归档）、总结。 - 会话区上方 ：手动压缩上下文、记忆与画像、专家包管理、提示词素材、任务清单、后台任务，再下面是那条用量栏。 - 输入区左下 ：「＋」模式与功能浮层——磨墨模式、头脑风暴、目标模式、定时任务，以及 @ 提及技能 / 工具 / MCP / 文件； 旁边依次是回复模式、审批模式、附件、专家包、模型、推理强度。 - 输入区右下 ：优化提示词、语音输入、发送。 Enter 发送， Shift+Enter 换行。 回复模式内置四档：智能、对话、经济、狂暴。差别在带不带工具目录、给几轮、追加哪段提示词； 自定义模式在 扩展 页管。 审批模式：四档 输入框左下那颗胶囊就是审批模式， 四档 ，随时可改，改的只是 这一场 ： id 标签 放行什么 拦住什么 --- --- --- --- ask 手动审批 读写本地文件等不走审批的工具 执行命令、访问网络，每一笔都先弹窗问你 auto 自动审批 命令与联网里没命中高危规则的 只命中高危规则那一类问你 full 完全访问 命令与联网一律不问 缺条件时仍会向你确认一次；灾难级命令照旧硬拦 night 夜间模式 命令、联网、提问全部不问 只拦灾难级命令 ask 是新对话的默认档。设置 → 审批模式 改的是 新对话的默认档 ；某一场挑过之后就不再跟随它。 terminal 执行命令、bg task 起后台任务（查状态 / 看日志 / 停止不改环境，不算）、 web search、web fetch、browser automation。读写本地文件不走这道门。 夜间模式到底是什么 它是 全托管 那一档：与完全访问同一条放行口径，外加把「缺条件时向你提一道选择题」也关掉。 遇到选择题不弹窗，直接让你从选项里自行拍板继续，并把选定的方案与理由写进回复。 它 不是 第四种放行规则，也不新开一套口子——差别只在「有没有任何东西在等人」。 配合「夜间模式运行任务时保持系统唤醒」（设置 → 审批模式，默认开着）过夜跑。 rm -rf / 、 rm -rf ~ 、 format c: 、 format d: 、 mkfs 、 dd if= 这几条前缀由后端无条件拒绝， 批准了也不放行。完全访问标红（没有安全网），夜间模式标夜紫（这一晚交给它）。 高危清单在哪 前后端各一份 同一条清单 ，两处都要改才对齐： - 前端： frontend/js/services/riskguard.js 的 HIGH RISK PATTERNS ，另加一条「下载后直接管给 shell」。 - 后端： backend/skills/terminal.py 的 HIGH RISK PATTERNS （多一条 PowerShell 的 ri 别名）与 BLOCKED PREFIXES 。 规则是写死的，覆盖删除文件与目录、磁盘写入与分区、关机重启、提权、强杀进程、注册表、服务与账户、 文件权限、Git 强推 / 硬重置 / 清理 / 删分支、数据库删表删库、卸载全局依赖。命令会先按 && 、 、 ; 、 拆段逐段检测，所以链式命令里藏一条也逃不掉。 审批框长什么样 标题分三种：高危命令审批 / 命令执行审批 / 联网访问审批。框里写清 触发规则 或当前档位， 列出那条命令或那个访问目标；命令类还会用当前模型解释它的目的（可在设置 → AI 辅助功能关掉）。 按钮是「批准执行」或「允许访问」。 并行时可能一次挤出好几张：它们 排队 ，后来的不会在你没看见之前被自动拒掉。 拒绝的理由会原样回给模型，并明确要求别再重试同一笔调用。 工具调用在界面上怎么呈现 每次调用是一张卡片：工具图标 + 名称 + 一句摘要 + 状态药丸。状态写的是 已执行 / 已应用 / 已创建 / 已追加 / diff 预览 / 文件预览 / 追加预览 / 失败 / 未执行 。 卡片默认 收起 ，只有失败的那张自动展开；点开看参数与输出。文件改动的参数只列文件路径与编辑条数， 不铺整份 diff。工具生成的图片、视频、文档会在卡片里直接给预览。 一次跑了好几笔会归成一组，标题写「调用 N 项」，后面列前三个工具名。 下一步 - 让 AI 在你不在场时接着干：办公室。 - 上下文预算怎么算：模型与用量。"},{"t":"团队 · 议事厅","u":"zh/06-team.html","s":"协作","h":["席位","一场讨论怎么跑","黑板工作流","每句话都留得下","下一步"],"x":"「团队」是顶栏里与「办公室」同级的一页，本身是一张桌子：几个人和几个 AI 席位在同一场讨论里，主持人推进轮次， 结论 由人签字 。界面并排三栏——左边在场席位、中间议事流、右边等你处理的事。 席位 - AI 席位 —— 从模型里挑，主持人安排谁先说、说几轮。 - 真人席位 —— 点「添加真人席位」发一张 票据 ，把入席链接发给对方。对方在自己的浏览器里 打开就能入席，看到的是 这一场 讨论，看不到你机器上的别的东西。 票据只决定\"这个人能进哪一场\"。它过期或作废时，对方页面会直接说 「票据已失效，请让主持人重新发一张」，不会静默卡在加载。 席位状态在左栏一目了然： 在线 、 暂离 、 未加入 、 超时未发言 。 谁没进来、谁掉线了，不用猜。 一场讨论怎么跑 1. 主持人开场，第一轮的席位开始发言，议事流里出现分隔尺 —— 第 1 轮 —— 。 2. 每一轮各席依次说话，可以「回应 {name}」点名接话。 3. 到终局轮，标题是 最终决策 ——这一条不是结论，是 等你拍板的提案 。 4. 停点那一行写「等待你拍板」，给你两个选择： 采纳拍板 或 继续讨论 。 采纳之后议事流里记「已采纳这个决策」，并把签字的人记进留痕。 真人席位可以配两件事： 权限 （能不能发言、能不能拍板），以及 等不到人怎么办 （让 AI 代笔 / 跳过并留痕 / 一直等，最后一种要填等多久）。邀请链接就在这个面板上发。 真人席位那一侧看到的措辞不一样：轮到他时提示「现在轮到你发言」， 提前打字会告诉他「发言会在轮到你时被采纳」，其余时间显示「等 {name} 发言…」。 他表态用的是这几种： 提案 、 支持 、 反对 、 反驳 、 补充 、 决策 。 只有你拍板的那一条算结论。夜间模式（全托管）下系统会替你采纳， 议事流里会明写「夜间模式：决策已自动采纳」——这一条是例外，不是默认。 黑板工作流 团队页也能跑黑板上的工作流：节点逐个执行，进度写成 {ok}/{n} 节点成功 ， 失败会停下来说明哪一步断掉，而不是把半截结果当成功。 每句话都留得下 发言、轮次、拍板、工具调用都落本地库，跟着备份一起走 （议事四张表在 项目与数据 里列了）。 换机器、恢复历史、或者把某场讨论单独清掉，都按那章的两种口径分开做。 下一步 - 想让活在你不在场的时候也被做完：办公室。 - 想看清每句话背后的工具调用：对话与审批。"},{"t":"办公室 · 招人、排班、交付","u":"zh/07-office.html","s":"办公室","h":["面板长什么样","招人","排班","交付队列","下一步"],"x":"办公室是 不同时刻 的协同：你留下一件活，AI 员工在他值班时做完，你回来验收。 它不新增一套后台服务—— 执行的是开着的 SLATE Teams 页面本身 。 顶栏「办公室」这一页默认落在 对话面 ；本章讲的是切到 工位 以后的这一面。 两面的切换在页面右上角，对话面与工位仍属于同一页。 后端只负责排队，不执行任何一件活。所以办公室需要有一台机器上的 SLATE Teams 是开着的， 那一个页面就是当班的人。关掉应用，活会安静地留在队列里，等下一次有页面在。 面板长什么样 左边是 花名册 和一张 工位平面图 （谁在忙、谁空着、谁在递话，一眼看得见）， 中间一个递话框可以直接「交给」某位、「贴出来」给所有人，或者「交办」一条活。 右边五页签： 动态 、 等你拍板 、 值班表 、 岗位 、 站会与绩效 。 这一章讲「岗位」和「值班表」，后两页在像人一样工作与门禁与账。 招人 「招聘」里两种来路： 按模板招一位 （内置四位：研究员、工程师、审校、值班管家）， 或者从零填一只新同事。一位员工身上你要定这几件事： 字段 它决定什么 --- --- 名字 / 头像 / 色相 同事之间靠名字寻址， 不能重名 岗位一句话 / 目标 / 职责 他干什么、朝哪儿使劲，也是分诊时判断\"该不该他办\"的依据 模型 / 轮数 / 项目 用哪只模型、一趟最多跑几轮、活落在哪个项目根 审校 他的交付要不要过人、由谁过；选「不设审校（交付直接给你）」就直接给你 每日预算 一天能花多少 token，花满就熔断（见门禁与账） 托管 他值班时按哪一档审批跑 不想要了按「解雇」——人从名册上走，他办过的活和说过的话 留在账上 ，绩效那一行标「已离职」。 排班 「新增值班」给一位员工排一条班。触发方式两类： - 每日定时 / 每隔几分钟 / 一次 —— 时钟到点就来看。 - 事件触发 —— 仓库有提交、盯的路径有文件变更、自检脚本变红、Git 推送、外部回调。 到点了 不等于要动 。每条班可以配 守卫条件 ，最常见的两条： - 「手上待办不超过几条」——0 的意思就是 手上没活才动 。 - 「只在某个时间窗里才排」。 守卫读不出条件、或者条件已不认识，都会在面板上写成一行原因，而不是默默跳过。 到点就动会让一个员工在上一件还没做完时又领一件，队列越堆越长。 守卫把\"该不该动\"变成一条可读到答案的检查。 交付队列 花名册上每位员工一个状态—— 空闲 、 在忙 、 下班 ——后面挂着几个计数： 待办、等你、待审校、退回、预算已满。活的状态是这几种，看得懂就够了： 状态 含义 --- --- 排队中 已排上，等一个开着的页面来领 在忙 有页面正拿着他在做（带租约，崩了会被重新领走） 待审校 做完了，等审校人过 等你 需要你拍板的事，列在「等你拍板」那一栏 受阻 卡住了，后面写着 受阻于什么 已定论 / 没跑成 做完了 / 跑坏了，坏因写在这一行 任何一件\"没办\"都必须有一行能被读到的原因——没有静默重试，也没有静默丢弃。 下一步 - 他怎么记得上次干到哪、怎么判断这活不该办：像人一样工作。 - 审校、预算、期限、站会与绩效：门禁与账。"},{"t":"办公室 · 像人一样工作","u":"zh/08-office-work.html","s":"办公室","h":["他记得上次","晨会分诊","判「不该办」要人点头","工位之间递话","下一步"],"x":"如果值班表只是\"到点叫一次模型\"，那它就是个定时任务。办公室这一层做的事，是让一个员工 记得上次、能自己排序、办不成要说原因、并且能把活递给同事 。 他记得上次 每位员工有一叠自己的备忘，用「给自己留备忘」写，只有他下次开工时读得到，分三类： - open —— 还没办完的事。 - ledger —— 一件事办完后的结论。 - blocked —— 缺什么条件才动得了。 开工时这三档按「未闭环 / 卡住 / 已定论」摆在他面前，最近的几条。 一件事真办完，得记一条 ledger 并 划掉 对应那条 open。不划掉，下一趟他会照原样再办一遍—— 这不是 bug，是\"记忆只记他写下的东西\"的直接后果。 晨会分诊 分诊是给 自己名下 的活逐条拍顺序，一次处理一批： 处置 意思 --- --- keep 该办。优先级 0–9，越大越先被领走；可以带一个要赶的时间点 defer 暂缓，改到明天再看 drop 判定这件事 不该办 ，必须写为什么 分诊只排自己的活，动不了别人的。 判「不该办」要人点头 员工可以判断一件事不该办，但 这个判断不生效 ：drop 之后那条活停在 「等你拍板」里，你有两个按钮： - 同意不该办，结案 —— 承认判断，活就此了结。 - 不对，放回队列 —— 推翻判断，它回到队列等下一次被领。 同样，办不下去时他用「把这一趟结掉」收口，状态只有两种，各自对应一扇门： - 受阻 —— 缺什么条件写在行上，你补上之后按「补齐条件，放回队列」。 - 判为不该办 —— 为什么写在行上，你点头才真的了结。 两种都要等人处理，不存在悄悄消失的活。 工位之间递话 「给同事递话」把一句话变成 排到对方名下的一条新活 ——不用等对方回话。收件人三种写法： - 同事的名字或工号； - user —— 只说给你听，会进你的通知； - broadcast —— 贴到办公室的动态流上，所有人都看得见。 一次只递一件事，写清楚要办什么，不贴过程。 递话是会计数的：动态流上标「第 1 手」「第 2 手」……数的是同事之间来回的次数。 到第 6 手就不再自动唤起任何人，只把话留下。这一条是防两个同事互相踢皮球踢到永远。 系统替喊的期限提醒不算一手——那是时钟，没有来回可言。 下一步 审校门禁、每日预算、期限升级、站会与绩效这四件\"管着\"的事，在 门禁与账。"},{"t":"办公室 · 门禁与账","u":"zh/09-office-gates.html","s":"办公室","h":["审校门禁","每日预算","期限过期会升级到人","两张卡","下一步"],"x":"放权给 AI 员工，要有几道闸：交付不能直接冲到你面前、钱要花得住、过期不能烂在桌上。 这四件事都在办公室这一层，且 全部从同一张队列表算出来 ，没有另记一份账。 审校门禁 招人的时候给一位员工选「审校人」，他的交付就先递给那位审校人， 不直接给你 。 - 审校本身是 一条排在审校人名下的活 ：它不该排在普通值班活后面，所以排得靠前一点， 但分诊抬了优先级的活仍然先走；期限默认两小时。 - 审校人用「判这一份交付」收口，只有两种判定： approve （合格，这份交付第一次递到你手上） 或 return （不合格，退回经办人重做，必须写要他改哪里）。 - 审校人必须是名册里的人， 不能审自己 ，也不能审一个已经不在名册的人。 没通过审校前，你只会看到「员工已交审校」；通过之后才是「员工交付」。 被退回时那一行写「审校退回：为什么」。这一条区分是刻意的—— 没过审的东西不该长得像交付 。 退回的重做走的是递话那条通道，所以一样数在「第 N 手」里，到 6 手止损。 每日预算 每位员工可以填一个 每日预算 （token）。今天花满之后： - 值班表 排不出新活 ，那条活会变成 受阻 ，行上写着为什么； - 晨会分诊和你手动交办的活 照样能排 ——否则预算一满，你连\"让他把手上最后一件做完\"都做不到。 绩效那一栏会写「{今天用的} / 上限 {预算}」，满了标一枚 预算已满 。 期限过期会升级到人 分诊时给一条活填了要赶的时间点，过期后 由时钟替人喊一句 ：议事流里出现一条系统提醒， 这条活进「等你拍板」。同一句提醒只喊一次，不会每刷新一次就催一遍； 一次最多升级几条，攒多了会把动态栏灌满——灌满等于没提醒。 两张卡 今日站会 —— 每个勾了「晨会分诊」的值班跑完，会在这一栏留一句自报：谁、说了什么、什么时候。 没人自报时它直接说\"给谁排一条勾了晨会分诊的值班\"，不放一张空表糊你。 绩效 —— 一人一行：办成几件、没跑成几件、待人几件、待审校几件、被退回几件、 一趟平均多久、今天用了多少 token。 那一栏量的是 从被领走到收口 那一段，不是端到端墙钟——活排队等多久不算在里面。 它给的是量级，不是凭证。 下一步 这些活、话、判定怎么进备份：项目与数据。"},{"t":"黑板与工作流","u":"zh/10-board.html","s":"能力","h":["卡片怎么连成逻辑链","黑板里的「工作流」视图","DAG 工作流在团队页跑","下一步"],"x":"黑板是顶栏第四个页签，一张 全局 的板：卡片、连线、笔迹、文字笔记四层叠在同一块画布上。 它不随对话分开，内容跟着本机设置一起存，换对话还在原地。 卡片怎么连成逻辑链 一张卡片四样东西： 标题 、 描述 、 颜色标签 、 箭头指向 （目标卡片 ID，多个用逗号分隔）。 双击任意卡片就地编辑，拖拽改位置，用工具栏的 连线 模式点两张卡片补一条边。 颜色不是装饰，每种带一个语义： 颜色 含义 --- --- 红色 风险 橙色 待处理 黄色 想法 绿色 完成 蓝色 信息 紫色 创意 默认 未分类 箭头表达依赖与数据流，看板视图按颜色分列、流程视图按箭头连成图、纲要视图按父子层级收成大纲、 Git 树读仓库提交。五个视图切换按钮就在黑板顶栏，默认落在 看板 。 工具栏另有画笔与文字两种自由层，配撤销笔画、清除所有笔；顶栏按钮是添加卡片、自动整理布局、 回到内容区、AI 整理成流程图、显示/隐藏流程图（Mermaid）、导出黑板、清空黑板。 「AI 整理成流程图」是AI 辅助功能里的一项（黑板 AI 整理）。 关掉它，这个按钮只说明原因，不会把整板内容发给模型。 黑板里的「工作流」视图 这一栏不是 DAG 编辑器，是一屏三件事： 1. 运行控制条 —— 当前状态写成 空闲 、 运行中 · 第 {n} 轮 、 已完成 、 已中断 ， 旁边是用时，按钮是停止、继续跑完、自动推进（开/关）、回复模式、思考强度、去团队。 这一场没跑过时，列表里留一行「本场还没有运行记录」，而不是留着上一场的尾巴。 2. 当前运行 —— 逐个列出本轮调用过的步骤，状态写 进行中 、 完成 、 失败 、 已取消 ， 标题带进度 当前运行 · {已完}/{总数} 。 3. 流程说明书卡片 —— 一份 Action 一张卡，写「共 {n} 步」「{n} 项输入」「产出落到哪儿」， 可就地展开步骤、点「运行此流程」（以 @提及 方式发进当前对话）、可置顶。 作者一栏分「用户编写」与「模型编写」。 底下还有 团队星图 ：中心是这一场对话，每个成员一颗行星，成员之间的真实交接画成弧。 本场没有团队记录时写「本场对话还没有团队记录」，并告诉你从哪儿发起。 DAG 工作流在团队页跑 真正按节点执行的工作流在团队页的 工作流 这一栏（与「团队讨论」并列的一张页签）。 - 定义是 JSON 文件，内置 8 份 放在 backend/workflows/ ；这一栏为空时界面直接写明放置路径。 - 跑之前要填任务需求，它作为 $input 传进每个节点；不填就停下来说「请先输入任务需求」。 - 节点行状态依次是 等待 / 运行中 / 成功 / 失败 / 跳过 ；无依赖关系的节点 同时执行 ， 进度写成 运行中（{done}/{n}）… 。 - 跑完的结果原文是 {ok}/{n} 节点成功 · 产物已写入知识库（{title}），可在记忆面板查看 。 节点都成功但写库失败时，写成 节点成功 {ok}/{n}，但写入知识库失败: {msg} —— 不会把半截结果报成成功 。 - 上游节点失败或跳过，下游自动跳过并写明是哪些上游带的；定义里有环时报 DAG 存在环，涉及节点: {nodes} ，这条工作流不执行。 - 节点既没绑定团队成员也没写死模型时，落在「AI 辅助功能 → 团队工作流执行」选的默认模型上； 绑定了的以绑定为准。绑不出可用模型的节点直接失败，不替你猜一只。 一份产物写成一条 工作流产物 · {工作流名} 的知识条目，含每个节点的状态、耗时、错误与产出摘要。 去记忆面板看，不在黑板上。 下一步 - Action 本身怎么建、怎么回滚：扩展。 - 工作流执行那一项的开关与默认模型：设置。"},{"t":"扩展","u":"zh/11-extensions.html","s":"能力","h":["技能与工具不是一回事","回复模式","专家包","MCP 与 Actions","下一步"],"x":"扩展是顶栏第五个页签，副标题一句话： 模型可用的能力在此页决定 。 左栏是一条分栏轨，七栏各带一个计数；轨上的数字与栏内标题上的数字同源，一处刷新两处一起变。 栏 管什么 你能做什么 --- --- --- 技能 一份写给模型的做事说明（SKILL.md） 新建、从本地路径导入、从 GitHub 仓库导入、扫描标准目录发现已装插件、删除、点开试跑 工具 后端常驻能力，模型经 skill run 调用 只读清单，点开可执行； 内置工具不可删除 模式 回复模式 内置四档只读，自定义可增改删 新功能 SLATE 自己生成的工具，放在 data/evolved/ 启用 / 停用、回滚到历史版本、撤销（删前先进历史） MCP 外部 MCP Server 带来的远程工具 添加、连接 / 断开、删除、按项目单独启停 专家包 角色设定 + 规则 + 知识库 + 技能打成一份包 新建、导入 zip、导出、增删包内文件 Actions 流程说明书 新建、编辑、删除、回滚 技能与工具不是一回事 技能 是一份 SKILL.md：你用自然语言写清\"遇到这类活怎么做\"，导入后模型按任务自己取用。 随产品带的示例技能有 6 份 （代码审查、提交信息、设计、调研、周报、Windows 排障）。 工具 是后端常驻的代码能力，这一栏列的是内置注册表里的 35 项 ——从读文件、改文件、跑终端、 后台任务，到生成 PPT/Word/Excel/PDF、浏览器与桌面自动化、联网搜索与网页获取。 它们只读、不可删除；你在界面上能关掉的，是设置里那些会自行调模型的功能： 关掉的功能连模型的工具目录都不会出现 。 另有一批对话内工具（读写黑板、工位递话、建回复模式、收口目标模式等）不在这张清单里单列， 由回复模式的工具白名单决定开不开。 用「工具工厂」（内置工具 mcp factory）生成一个，产物落在 data/evolved/ ， 出现在 新功能 这一栏，随时可停用、回滚、撤销。每次覆盖、撤销、回滚都先存入历史版本，最多留 5 版。 回复模式 回复模式决定 这一场对话用哪套提示词、开放哪些工具、跑几轮、思考强度多高、用哪只模型 。 内置四档只读： 智能 （带全套工具）、 对话 （不给工具，一轮就停）、 经济 （只给只读工具、 低强度、12 轮）、 狂暴 （全套工具、高强度、40 轮，中途不停下来等确认）。 自定义模式是一份完整规格：id、显示名、图标、颜色、追加提示词、工具白名单（逐格勾）、 推理强度、轮数上限、指定模型（默认跟随当前主模型）。模型自己也能建模式——它调 mode write 工具，落点与你手动建的是同一份注册表。 在输入框上方改的是 这一场用哪个模式 ；在扩展页「模式」栏改的是 模式本身长什么样 。 删除一个正在被使用的自定义模式不会崩，用到它的会话回落到默认模式。 审批模式（手动 / 自动 / 完全访问 / 夜间）是另一套东西，管的是 命令与联网要不要问你 ， 在设置页里定默认档，见对话与审批。 专家包 一份专家包 = 人格设定 + 行为规则 + 知识库文件 + 技能文件，打成一个可切换的整体。 随产品带的示例包有 3 份 。用法两条：对话时在下方的专家包选择器里选一份注入这一场； 在团队里则挂到某个 AI 席位上。 MCP 与 Actions MCP 这一栏连的是外部 Server，连上后它的远程工具进入模型视野；与内置同名的远程工具由内置接管。 每台服务器可以全局停用，也可以只对当前项目单独启用或停用（项目掩码），摘掉掩码就回到全局配置。 Actions 是一份份 流程说明书 ：把常规操作写成必需步骤，模型按流程执行。 存成 data/actions/<id .yml ，也可以放进项目自己的 .slate/actions/ ——项目里同名的那份优先。 每次覆盖都留底，最多 5 版，可回滚；解析不了的旧版本不允许盖回去。 在黑板的工作流视图里，一份 Action 就是一张可就地运行的卡片。 下一步 - 哪些功能会自行调模型、怎么逐项关掉：设置。"},{"t":"项目、备份与账本","u":"zh/12-projects-data.html","s":"数据与设置","h":["项目与工作区","备份里到底有什么","恢复时的两个顺序坑","两种\"清空\"不是一回事","故意不进这份 JSON 的东西","下一步"],"x":"Teams 的东西分三层： 视野 （正在看哪个项目）、 记录 （对话数据库里的表）、 配置 （ data/ 下那些文件与项目里的 .slate/ ）。一次备份只搬得动前两层的一半。 项目与工作区 - 单目录项目 ：项目路径就是那个目录。 工作区 ：一个宿主目录存配置，成员是若干彼此无关的文件夹。 - 工作区的宿主目录落在 data/workspaces/<名字 ，配置写在它的 .slate/config.json 里，只有三样： 性质、成员清单、当前根。成员写相对路径时按宿主目录解析，所以整个工作区连配置拷走也不散架。 - 当前根 任何时刻只有一个：切根只改配置里那一项，文件、Git、终端的工作目录跟着一起换。 配置的读写位置另记一处，所以工作区的配置不会被串改进某个成员自己的 .slate/ 。 - 在册的项目全部留在 data/projects.json ， 正在看的那一个 仍是唯一的。项目身份由宿主目录的 绝对路径派生——目录搬走身份就变，所以每条记录还带一份别名，供你手工把老会话归回来。 - 会话按项目 id 认归属，不按名字：改名、重名、搬家都不该把历史甩出去。 - SLATE 私有的每项目数据在 data/projects/<id / ，绝不写进你的仓库。 备份里到底有什么 导出是一个 JSON（带版本号），三段：后端表、浏览器本地那一份、团队历史列表。后端那三段是这些表： 段 表 装的是什么 --- --- --- 对话 conversations、messages 会话与消息，含归档过的 记忆与素材 memories、prompt snippets 长期记忆、提示词素材 议事四张 team sessions、team turns、team attendees、team inbox 每场的行头与名册快照、发言全文、票据（只存 sha256）、待代收的发言 账本两张 runs、tool events 每一趟的账与工具调用事件；星图与\"这一轮改了哪些文件\"都从这份数 办公室两张 office jobs、office messages 交付队列与工位传话 按天记账 daily usage 每天的 token；少了它，恢复完会话齐全而活跃度热力图一片空白 名册三张 employees、employee duties、employee notes 员工、值班表、他自己的备忘 少一张的症状永远一样： 备份看着齐全，恢复后那一块全空 。所以新增一张表必须当场表态 它是记录还是配置——归进哪一份清单，不表态就有自检脚本判红。 恢复时的两个顺序坑 - 先建表，再合并 。议事、账本与办公室的表都由各自端点首次触达时才惰性建起来；一台从没开过 团队、也从没招过员工的干净机器上它们根本不存在。导入前不建，存在性检查会把这些一律当成 \"没数据\"跳过——报 0 条，界面照样说\"恢复完成\"。 - 只并新，不覆盖 。按主键或自然键插入，已存在的整行跳过；想拿备份盖掉现有内容，这条路不走。 发言与工具事件两张还要丢掉自带的行号再插：同一笔发言在两台机器上是同一个（场次，序号）， 照搬会撞上本地新写的那行并被静默吞掉。 - 导入完成后页面会重载一次，本地那半截要重载才生效。 两种\"清空\"不是一回事 你点的地方 清掉了 留着 --- --- --- 侧栏「任务」→ 管理 → 清空全部 会话与消息 议事正文、交付历史、名册与值班表；只把指向这些会话的引用抹空 设置 → 存储空间 → 清空对话 会话、消息、议事四张、账本两张、办公室那两张、按天记账，随后压缩数据库 员工、值班表、他自己的备忘；记忆与素材；知识库 确认框里就得把这句话写全，只说一句\"清空对话\"是骗人。名册与班是 配置 ，不是对话记录， 所以一个人说\"清空对话\"时不该顺手解雇员工、取消他的班。 故意不进这份 JSON 的东西 data/ 下的配置与二进制一概不在备份里：桌面共享设置 desktop state.json 、MCP 的端点与密钥 mcp servers.json 、定时任务 scheduled tasks.json 、自定义技能 skills/ 、专家包 experts/ 、 流程说明书 actions/ 、全局宪法 constitution.json 、知识库 knowledge.db 、背景图与导入字体 data/theme/ 、在册清单与工作区宿主 projects.json 、 workspaces/ 。 项目自己那份 <项目 /.slate/ 跟着代码库走，本来就不该进备份。 本地那半截里带着你填过的模型 Key。别提交进仓库，别发到群里。 下一步 - 换台机器接着干：手机遥控。 - 备份没装进去的那些开关在哪：设置页有什么。 - 踩了坑再回来查：常见问题。"},{"t":"手机遥控","u":"zh/13-mobile.html","s":"数据与设置","h":["手机上有什么","手机上没有什么","怎么进手机界面","遥控开关在哪拨","地址怎么拿","无界面模式","为什么只换脸","下一步"],"x":"遥控是 同一套后端的另一张脸 ：手机浏览器连的是你机器上那个后端，跑的还是同一台引擎。 它不新增服务，也不新增第二种执行方式。 手机上有什么 五个页签： 对话 、 会话 、 记忆 、 待办 、 设置 。 - 对话里流式续写、思考折叠、工具卡片都在；工具真能改文件（写文件、改文件、追加都走同一批接口）。 - 审批换成了底部弹层：高危命令与文件变更照样要你点头，改动先给一份 diff 预览再决定接受还是拒绝。 - 设置里四件事：遥控地址与二维码、选模型、填密钥、切主题。 - 这一趟结束后，后台任务的完成事件也照样被读回来。 手机上没有什么 团队、办公室、黑板、扩展 这四个页签只在桌面上。所以： - 手机上开不了议事厅，也看不见交付队列；与会者拿票据进的是另一页（只有那一场讨论）， 不是工作台——把他领进整套工作台只会让他看到一片被拒的请求。 - 手机页面 不领办公室的活 。后端只排队不执行，而当班的是桌面上那个开着的页面； 只有手机在线、桌面全关着，员工的活会安静地留在队列里。 文件、Git、终端、账本全在你那台主机上。主机睡了，手机那边没人替你干活。 怎么进手机界面 带授权码的地址在手机浏览器里打开后，界面按移动 UA 自动分流到为触屏重排的那一页， 地址后面的授权码原样保留。不想用移动版就在地址后面加 slate mobile=0 回到桌面版。 遥控开关在哪拨 设置 → 局域网遥控 → 启用局域网遥控 ，就这一处。 - 偏好记在本机 data/desktop state.json ；文件不在、读坏了、没这个键，一律按\"开\"处理。 - 关掉是 真的把局域网那个监听端口释放掉 ，不是把地址藏起来。 - 这个开关 只能在主机上拨 。从遥控端口拨过来会被拒——你正靠这条连接做事，关掉等于把自己 关在门外；而\"打开\"方向在服务停掉之后根本不可达。 地址怎么拿 主机那一块设置里列出带授权码的地址，可以直接复制，也可以扫码。地址由本机局域网 IP 和 副服务 实际抢到的端口 拼出来：首选端口被占就向上让，所以别把端口写死在别处。 主授权码是每次进程起来时新生成的一份，重启就换。手机上的旧地址会停在\"需要授权\"那一页， 回到主机的设置里再复制一次即可。 无界面模式 给没有桌面环境的机器用的（服务器、树莓派、容器）：不开窗口、不起托盘，只起后端与局域网遥控， 然后把本机地址和带授权码的遥控地址打到终端，按 Ctrl+C 收尾。 - 它强制 本次进程 开启遥控，不写进偏好文件；也不复用别人已经起好的后端——远程模式下 手上没有界面可以补救，必须保证这次一定有遥控。 - 后端起不来时把原因写在终端，细节留给 desktop backend.log ；没有窗口可以承载失败页。 为什么只换脸 工具循环、消息组装、审批判定、渲染逻辑都在桌面上那份服务模块里，手机这一侧只注入自己的 视图与输入。两张脸共用一颗引擎，是为了不出现\"手机上看着能做、其实做的是另一套\"。 代价也很实在：议事与办公室的交互搬不进触屏，就干脆不搬，页签在手机上直接不存在。 下一步 - 票据与被收窄的作用域：团队 · 议事厅。 - 为什么活要等一个开着的页面：办公室。 - 备份里没带上这些开关：项目、备份与账本。"},{"t":"设置","u":"zh/14-settings.html","s":"数据与设置","h":["模型与上下文","自定义主题","AI 辅助功能","能力为什么不在这里管","数据与设备"],"x":"设置是顶栏第五个页签。左栏一份锚点导航、上方一个搜索框，右栏是分组区块； 导航条目由页面现读区块生成 ，所以组数随版本变，但顺序与主区始终一致。当前共 21 组 ： 模型配置 · API 测试 · 用量统计 · 上下文与项目 · 自动推进 · AI 辅助功能 · 通知 · 后台任务 · 多任务与项目 · 通用 UI（实验性）· 自定义主题 · 联网搜索 · 图片生成 · 视频生成 · 审批模式 · 数据备份与恢复 · 会话归档 · 存储空间 · 局域网遥控 · 打字小游戏 · 关于。 改完点右上角 保存 统一落盘。界面语言 不在这里 ：它在安装时选定（写入 data/language.txt ）， 应用内不切换，优先级是环境变量 SLATE LANG 该文件 默认中文。 模型与上下文 模型配置 里两件事：自定义模型（名称/ID、请求模式 OpenAI 兼容 / Anthropic / curl 直连、 Base URL、API Key、Context Window）和内置模型密钥。下面还有一条可选的 Responses API 开关。 API 测试 用一条最短请求打一次真实链路——它走的就是对话那条路，不是另造一条。 上下文与项目 这组决定模型一次能看到多少： - 上下文 Token 上限：内置模型与已填窗口的模型走「自动」，各取标称窗口的八成； 这一档只给完全没有窗口信息的模型兜底。要单独调某只模型，用模型配置里那一行的「最大上下文」—— 滑杆粗选、旁边的数字框可填精确值、本地与自定义端点还能 探测窗口 。压缩阈值与上下文条按同一个数算。 - 单次输出上限（1024–65536）；默认勾上「输出文件时把长度上限提升到 65536，避免大文件被截断」。 - 默认勾上「自动确认文件创建与修改」；关掉后恢复成写文件前先预览、点接受。 - 项目宪法 ：这一项目里长期有效的硬规则。同组还有提示词工厂的入口。 自定义主题 启用自定义主题后，配色 只填四个源色 （页面底色、面板底色、正文、强调），其余色值由它们按亮度 与对比度算出来——正文与三个次要层级都会被拉到能读的清。预设色板有 10 档 ： 簿纸、墨夜、雾蓝、深海、松墨、苔绿、陶土、暮紫、石墨、铅字。点一个预设就把整套源色填进色板， 之后仍可逐格改； 改过之后这一份就不再属于任何预设 。 自定义主题开启时，顶栏的明暗按钮与 Ctrl+D 不生效，点它会说明原因。关闭自定义主题，整套回到内置主题。 - 字体 ：系统已装的字体族按名字直接用；「导入字体」只收单个 .woff2 / .woff / .ttf / .otf （16MB 以内），文件 只落在本机 data/theme/fonts/ ——不进对话记录、不进仓库、不进安装包， 也不会跟着备份到另一台机器。只导入一个字重时，粗体与斜体由浏览器模拟。 - 板块透明度 （55%–100%）是面板、卡片、输入框与助手气泡那一层底色的 平面不透明度 ， 调低透出的是页面底色或背景图， 不是毛玻璃模糊 ；用户自己的气泡与代码块始终实色。 - 背景图 存在本机 data/theme/ ，配一条遮罩浓度（40%–95%）：过低会让正文压在图上，过高等于没铺图。 Wallpaper Engine 那栏只读取它自己目录里的配置与 preview 图，取来当背景图——不启动它、也不改它的设置。 AI 辅助功能 除对话、团队讨论、提示词工厂外，所有会 自行调用模型 的功能都在这一组：共 15 项 ， 逐项开关，其中 12 项 还能各选一只模型。剩下三项不带模型栏，因为模型另有归属： 定时与事件任务的模型 在每个任务里各自选 ，图片生成与视频生成的模型与 Key 在各自区块配置。 关掉一项，就不再为它发任何请求。 覆盖的是：上下文压缩摘要、记忆自动蒸馏、记忆手动提取、对话洞察捕获、自动会话标题、 代码理解文档、代码审查、黑板 AI 整理、提示词优化、子代理并行、高危命令目的说明、团队工作流执行。 「自动推进」的审阅模型和「后台任务」的自动续跑在各自区块里设，这里不重复列。 能力为什么不在这里管 工具、技能、回复模式、专家包、MCP、Actions 全部在扩展页——那里是能力清单的 唯一一处真相 。设置页只留两类东西：能力的 供应商配置 （联网搜索引擎与渲染方式、图片/视频生成的 模型与 Key）和能力的 调用闸门 （上面那 15 项开关）。同一件事在两处各管一半，不会各说各话。 这组里定的是新对话的默认 审批模式 （手动 / 自动 / 完全访问 / 夜间）； 回复模式 是另一回事，在输入框上方按场挑。 数据与设备 数据备份与恢复 导出单个 JSON（对话、议事与账本、员工名册与值班表、记忆、素材、设置）， 恢复按 id 合并、不覆盖已有数据；细目见项目与数据。 会话归档 放从「任务」栏归档的会话，可恢复可彻底删除。 存储空间 可压缩数据库、清缓存。 局域网遥控 开一个本机地址给手机或平板，用法见移动端。"},{"t":"常见问题","u":"zh/15-faq.html","s":"数据与设置","h":["起不来、连不上","界面","办公室与议事","数据","下一步"],"x":"每一条都能回到源码里的某一句判据。没把握的事不在这儿。 起不来、连不上 双击没反应，或者后端起不来。 第一份实例还在开窗口、或者藏在通知区域里时，再双击一次会把 它叫回来，终端里回你一句\"已在运行\"。真起不来时端口多半被占：应用首选 8130，被占就自己退到 一个空闲口；遥控那侧首选 8131，被占就向上试二十个。两边都按 实际拿到的口 走，界面上的地址 就是真相，别处不用改。 日志在哪个文件。 后端与启动过程写 desktop backend.log ：源码跑在仓库根，Windows 装机版在 程序目录旁边，macOS 装机版挪进了数据目录。页面上抛出来的错误另记一份在 data/js errors.log 。 手机打开地址被拦在\"需要授权\"，或者昨天还能连今天连不上。 前者是地址里没带授权码——回主机的 设置里复制或扫码。后者是主授权码每次进程起来时都换一把，重启之后要重新复制一次。 为安全起见，不带授权码的局域网访问一律拦下。 界面 界面语言怎么切。 应用内不切：语言在安装时选定，写进 data/language.txt 。要换就把那个文件 改成 en 或 zh ，或者用环境变量 SLATE LANG 盖一次，然后重启。 深色下红墨那一侧对比不够。 报警红、完成绿、待办橙这些语义色不是跟着你的强调色走的： 浅色与深色各备一套值，页面按背景的亮度挑一套，自定义主题也不例外。红墨在浅色下深而钝、 在深色下换成更亮的一档，就是为了不让\"越浓越看不见\"发生在深色里。 办公室与议事 员工的活为什么不跑。 后端只排队，不执行任何一件活——当班的是那台机器上 开着的页面 。 页面全关着，活就留在队列里；租约过期自动退回排队，同一条最多被领两次，第二次还死掉就判失败。 手机上没有办公室，所以手机不当班。 被判\"不该办\"之后，活去哪了。 进「等你拍板」那一栏，理由写在这一行上。它不算失败，也不由 后端自行复活：只有两条出口——你把它放回队列（优先级抬到高于普通值班活，分诊仍能排到它前面）， 或者你同意这确实不该办、落成结案。员工自己推不开这扇门。 每日预算满了，为什么我手动交办还能排。 熔断只回答\"还排不排 新的值班活 \"。已经排队的照旧 办完（半路掐了更贵也更难解释），晨会分诊照排——那正是\"剩这点预算该干什么\"的判断本身； 你按下那一下照排，由人负责。 备忘为什么下一趟又办了一遍。 那条\"未闭环\"没被划掉。让他写新备忘时带上要划掉的那条编号； 每人只留最近四十条，不设上限的话他自己的历史迟早把窗口撑爆。 与会者那一页说票据失效。 让主持人重签一张。票据可以被撤回，库里只留它的哈希，所以撤回之后 那张链接永久作废——原文没法从备份里读回来。 数据 \"清空对话\"之后员工还在，恢复备份却报 0 条。 两个都是设计： 名册、值班表与员工备忘算配置 ， 不在清空那一刀里。 报 0 条 要看那份备份里本来有没有这块数据——导入前会先把议事与办公室的表 建出来，就是为了不在干净机器上把整块历史静默丢掉；早期版本导出的备份根本没带那几组表， 重新导出一次才有。 备份里有我的 Key 吗。 后端那半截（数据库里的表）没有；本地那半截是明文， 带着你填过的模型 密钥 。反过来， data/ 下的配置与二进制都不进备份：桌面共享设置、MCP 端点与密钥、定时任务、 技能、专家包、流程说明书、全局宪法、知识库、背景图与导入字体。换机器时这些要自己搬。 下一步 - 三种装法与端口分配：安装与启动。 - 备份的完整口径：项目、备份与账本。 - 遥控与无界面模式：手机遥控。"}]};
